d","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":13,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Assessed all assigned scope selectors, the live DEF, canonical artifact, cited evidence available in the repository, and applicable upstream designs. Three scope and traceability defects require correction. No authored/generated visual is present or necessary to assess this epic-level capability definition.","findings":[{"id":"scope-order-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/4/dependsOn","message":"Story s5 removes answer-layout limits but depends only on s1, allowing it to run before measured sizing and complete handling exist. This contradicts FR004 and the explicit non-goal prohibiting removal of any limit before the analyzer can handle what it admits. Make layout-limit removal depend on the relevant sizing/handling capabilities, or separate layout selection from uncapping with an explicit prerequisite.","evidenceReferences":["DEF.md:32 — FR004 prohibits removing limits before handling exists","DEF.md:101 — non-goal requires completeness, measurement and handling before limit removal","DEF.md:194-201 — s5 depends only on s1 and removes all layout finding limits",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/4"]},{"id":"scope-budget-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8","message":"Story s9 introduces aggregate child-task limits and an execution budget without defining how coverage survives reaching them. It also prohibits large child plans for L/XL requests, whereas the applicable upstream design explicitly uses L-sized child plans to cover XL partitions. The DEF simultaneously requires processing every part with no findings lost and excludes reducing time/model cost. Specify the intended replacement depth policy and whether budget exhaustion causes incomplete failure, resumable continuation, or coverage-preserving replanning; distinguish that behavior from successful complete analysis.","evidenceReferences":["DEF.md:89 — reducing time/model usage is a non-goal","DEF.md:108-109 — k1 and k2 require accuracy and lossless inclusion","DEF.md:161-167 — s3 requires complete processing and combination","DEF.md:265-269 — s9 introduces shallow child plans, task limits and execution budgets","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:155-194 — XL partitions normally spawn L child plans","design/analyze-framework.md:42-46 — five-bucket depth and coverage policy"]},{"id":"scope-citation-03","severity":"MED","location":"/citations/20/id","message":"Citation id c21 is duplicated: index 18 identifies the historical unfocused-request failure, while index 20 identifies the Redis/etcd sampling decision. Consequently, the assumption and s6/s7 references to c21 cannot resolve uniquely and may select unrelated evidence. Give the sampling decision a distinct id and update its references while preserving the failure evidence identity.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/18",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/20",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/assumptions/3/source","DEF.md:215,232,291,293 — c21 references and conflicting definitions"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/flavor","/body/problem","/body/nonGoals","/body/assumptions","/body/constraints","/body/stories","/body/openQuestions","/body/functionalDefinition","document:line:26","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/3","/body/constraints/4","/body/constraints/5","/body/constraints/6","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/citations/9","/citations/10","/citations/11","/citations/12","/citations/13","/citations/14","/citations/15","/citations/16","/citations/17","/citations/18","/citations/19","/citations/20","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-context-builder.md — lossless relevance window, failure modes and cache policy","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — contracts, validation, recursive plans and failure propagation","design/analyze-framework.md — scope buckets and root depth ceilings","CLAUDE.md — accuracy, serial model calls, trailing structural reference and analyzer steering","site/analyze.html:61 — exploration-grounded claims",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-12f70133491114c9.json — excluded graph repairs","src/analyze/explore — cited lookup constants, content cuts and completeness reporting","src/analyze/runtimes/data/discovery-objects.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/infra/_shared.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/infra/discovery-families.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/code/adherence-check.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/data/adherence-check.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/infra/adherence-check.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/docs/family-summarise.ts","src/analyze/docs-retrieval.ts","src/analyze/summariser/driver.ts","src/analyze/planner/schema.ts","src/analyze/planner/scope-band.ts","src/analyze/measure.ts","src/analyze/context/driver.ts","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.code.system.md","src/daemon/tools/builtins/search/grep.ts","src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts","git commit 83a1cc0 — steering-only change","git history for src/analyze/classifier/scope-picker.ts and src/mcp/analyze-step/phases/start.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Extend the functional-definition representation to cover s8 and s9; its current item requirements stop at s7, leaving the newer capabilities without stable requirement identifiers.","Label the problem statement and c2/c11 code references as the historical baseline. Their cited files no longer exist at those paths, and current measurement and broad-request handling already implement parts of the proposed behavior.","Retain the explicit boundaries for graph repair, index freshness, live-store sampling and general-purpose tool callers when refining acceptance criteria. Historical external logs and live-run observations were assessed as recorded evidence; replaying those measurements is optional for this scope review."]},{"chunkId":"broad","status":"passed","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the live DEF, canonical requirements, upstream designs and relevant runtime/test sources. The s6–s8 boundaries are feasible: context entry precedes lifecycle execution, directory-module support completes the code-family path, and s3 explicitly closes the accepted docs aggregation exception. No blocking design defect was demonstrated. No authored or generated visual is attached to this DEF; its epic-level interactions and ownership requirements are adequately expressed in prose.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/5","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/6","/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/7","/body/stories/7/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/7/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/7/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/7/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/7/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/6","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/27","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/28","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/29","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/30","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/31","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","DEF.md sections 6.6–6.8 — context entry, lifecycle, module discovery and compatibility acceptance","DEF.md section 2, S007:FR003 — docs aggregation exception and code-family dependency","DEF.md section 6.3, ac7 — closure of the docs aggregation exception","design/analyze-context-builder.md:69-183 — bundle ownership, broad context, caching and distinct failure causes","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:63-83,155-194,248-266 — nested report materialization, serial execution, persistence and partial failures","design/analyze-framework-code.md:5-20,39-69 — code scopes, discovery and functional-surface expectations","src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1590-1675 — unfocused run-mode entry and cause-specific pipeline failures","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:153-207,254-329 — terminal failures, stored-result retrieval and source-hinted entry","src/analyze/orchestrator/persistence.ts:103-136 — abandoned-run terminal records","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts:340-390 — nested execution and child report materialization","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/source-modules.ts — directory identity, stored-module ownership, path normalization and invalid values","src/analyze/runtimes/code/discovery-modules.ts — shared module definition and discovery output","src/analyze/runtimes/code/structure-module-tree.ts — module nodes, file ownership and import-edge contracts","src/analyze/runtimes/code/surface-functional.ts — directory and entity-id inputs, recursive surface and explicit refusals","src/analyze/runtimes/code/__tests__/module-directories.test.ts:128-185,363-535 — discovery, ownership, compatibility and invalid-module scenarios","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/hinted-branch.test.ts:68-100 — focused and unfocused source-hinted requests","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/shaper-causes.test.ts:56 — cause-specific failures and recorded terminal output","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/orchestrator.test.ts:489-540 — completed-run replay assertions","src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-run-abandoned.test.ts — observable abandonment and terminal-record preservation scenarios","src/indexer/parser/go.ts:376-391 — imported-module entities use an empty repository/file","src/indexer/parser/python.ts:223-235 — imported-module entities use an empty repository/file"],"limitations":[],"advice":["When refining acceptance fixtures, explicitly cover mixed-language directories, source only in descendants, overlapping stored modules, and relative versus absolute module values. The current shared runtime supplies concrete identity and ownership rules that can anchor those fixtures.","Keep completion evidence distinct from report existence: verify nested results reach the report and inspect functional-surface task statuses, as s7/ac2 and s8/ac5 require.","Tests and live analyses were not executed; this read-only DEF assessment inspected their source contracts and assertions."]},{"chunkId":"reporting","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned reporting selectors were assessed. Failure distinction, partial-read reporting, evidence preservation and prohibition of silent answer fallback are coherent and feasible on both paths. One acceptance criterion conflicts with retained sampling and unknown-total results. No additional visual artifact is necessary for this epic-level capability.","findings":[{"id":"reporting-unknown-total-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/0","message":"ac1 requires every incomplete lookup or analysis step to report how many results exist, without allowing an unknown total. This cannot be satisfied for unreadable sources, searches stopped before enumeration finishes, or the Redis/etcd samples explicitly retained by s4/ac6 without scanning every key. It also conflicts with the current result contract, which correctly permits total: null. Require exact totals when established; otherwise require an explicit unknown total and its reason, alongside the returned count and completeness basis. This makes s1 independently acceptable before limits are removed and avoids encouraging fabricated counts or prohibited full scans.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:126 — unconditional total requirement","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:186 — sampled Redis/etcd listings remain incomplete and must not scan every key","src/analyze/completeness.ts:61-70 — Completeness.total explicitly permits null","src/analyze/explore/completeness-facts.ts:101-117 — stopped text searches cannot establish the total","src/analyze/explore/__tests__/completeness-all-lookups.test.ts:387,431 — document and stopped-search fixtures assert unknown totals"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/5","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/0","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/7","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/8","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/9","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/10","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/11","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/6","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-context-builder.md — bundle ownership, lossless context and failure surfaces","design/analyze-framework.md:245-270 — task failures, absent producers and aggregation provenance","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:248-266 — resumability and partial child-plan failure","site/analyze.html:38-61 — analyzer entry points and exploration-grounded claims","src/analyze/completeness.ts — result contracts, derived answer reports and incomplete-source reasons","src/analyze/explore/completeness-facts.ts — graph-relative completeness, exclusion rules and unknown totals","src/analyze/explore/answer-report.ts — failed, unsupported and missing-record propagation","src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1735-1855 — exploration preservation and terminal synthesis failures","src/analyze/context/synthesizer.ts — evidence-only synthesis and typed answer failures","src/analyze/context/answer-step-error.ts — retained lookup results, upstream inputs and failure causes","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts:264-334 — task failure and completeness-record enforcement","src/daemon/steps/analyze-step/phases/bundle.ts — independently derived reports and terminal invalid-answer evidence","src/analyze/runtimes/data/discovery-objects.ts — driver listing cuts and unknown totals","src/analyze/__tests__/completeness.test.ts — complete-empty, incomplete, failed and partly-read contract assertions","src/analyze/explore/__tests__/completeness-all-lookups.test.ts — lookup coverage and known/unknown count assertions","src/daemon/steps/__tests__/analyze-step-bundle-report.test.ts — derived report and forged-completeness rejection assertions","src/daemon/steps/__tests__/analyze-step-answer-prompt-missing.test.ts — plan/narrow failure evidence preservation","src/analyze/context/__tests__/answer-failure-mapping.test.ts — daemon and plan-tree failure payload preservation","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.code.system.md — failed lookup diagnostics and freeform completeness basis","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.adherence.system.md — incomplete text evidence diagnostics","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.data.system.md — failed versus complete-empty listings"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Make graph-relative completeness and sampled-source incompleteness explicit fixtures for s1/ac5, retaining the DEF's graph-repair non-goal.","Tests and live analyses were not executed; this read-only DEF assessment inspected relevant contracts and test assertions."]},{"chunkId":"sizing","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Measured sizing covers both paths, caller hints, reporting and conservative unknown-size fallback. Story s9 lacks prerequisites and leaves bounded execution, aggregate limits and timing acceptance insufficiently defined.","findings":[{"id":"sizing-prerequisites-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8","message":"Story s9 has no dependsOn declaration although its criteria require measured sizes supplied by s2 and an executable broad-analysis path supplied by s7. The tracked ordering therefore permits s9 before its prerequisites. Declare those dependencies and identify any complete-handling prerequisite needed for its end-to-end docs criterion.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8 — no dependsOn field","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:139 — s2 prerequisites","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:225 — s7 provides broad execution","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:167 — s3 closes oversized docs aggregation"]},{"id":"sizing-budget-completeness-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","message":"Reporting that an execution budget was reached does not define what happens to unfinished coverage, completed findings or the final report. A bounded run can satisfy ac4 while abandoning work required by s3 and k2. Define the observable terminal outcome, retained findings and uncovered work, and whether continuation or coverage-preserving replanning completes the request. Distinguish budget exhaustion from successful complete analysis. Also reconcile ac1's prohibition on large child plans with the upstream XL policy that explicitly uses L-sized children; measured child sizes must not be relabelled merely to fit a budget.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:265-268","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:161-167 — whole-request handling and lossless combination",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/constraints/0",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/constraints/1",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/constraints/2","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — XL → planner-template tasks and Failure surface","src/analyze/planner/recursive.ts:158 — child size is measured independently"]},{"id":"sizing-aggregate-policy-03","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/2","message":"The aggregate rejection criterion refers to a total and what the request's size allows, but neither the counted resource nor the governing aggregate policy is identified. Existing task-count bands apply separately to each plan, and the existing root depth ceiling does not bound the sum of child tasks. Specify what is totalled, which descendants and root work count, and which size-based policy governs rejection and execution. Cover XS explicitly or state that its existing policy is retained; ac1 and ac2 currently cover only four of the five supported sizes.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:265-268","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — invariant 13 applies to each individual plan","design/analyze-framework.md:42-46 — five supported size policies","src/analyze/planner/scope-band.ts — per-plan task-count bands","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:159 — taskCountFailure checks plan.tasks.length","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:209 — separate root-scope depth ceiling"]},{"id":"sizing-timing-acceptance-04","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","message":"“Within a stated time” supplies no acceptance threshold or rule for establishing one before execution. Any completed run can pass by stating a time above its observed duration, so this does not test the story's promised reasonable completion time. Identify the broad docs request and repository fixture or revision, establish the time target and relevant execution conditions before the run, and define the measured interval. Retain the required depth and task-count records alongside that result.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:261 — reasonable completion time is the stated user value","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:269 — no timing threshold, request fixture or execution conditions"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/8","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/1","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/12","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/13","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-plan-builder.md","design/analyze-framework.md — scope policies and root depth ceiling","design/analyze-context-builder.md — Sizing","docs/daemon.md — How a request's size is measured","src/analyze/classifier/driver.ts — unsized classifier contract","src/analyze/measure.ts — count mapping, hints, unknown fallback and sampled sources","src/mcp/server.ts — structured request and sizeHint schema","src/daemon/steps/analyze-step/phases/start.ts — measurement before planning","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts — measurement and planner handoff","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts — measured-size stamping and depth ceiling","src/analyze/planner/recursive.ts — nested planning and child measurement","src/analyze/planner/scope-band.ts","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts — per-plan count validation","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts — serial execution and task records","src/analyze/__tests__/measure.test.ts — sizing boundaries and monotonicity","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/run-measure.test.ts — measured-size planner integration"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Link s9 explicitly to the functional requirements it extends and the constraints its acceptance criteria operationalize.","Preserve the documented Redis/etcd exception: report sampling and unknown measurements, use XL conservatively, and avoid a full key scan.","No authored or generated visual is attached to these assigned capabilities; the DEF-level sizing requirements can be assessed in prose. Tests and live timing runs were not executed during this read-only design review."]},{"chunkId":"handling","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed. Partition coverage, retained findings, partial failures, sequential model calls and closure of the docs aggregation exception are coherent at DEF level. One acceptance criterion incorrectly prohibits partitioning small requests whose content exceeds model capacity. No additional visual artifact is necessary for this capability at this stage.","findings":[{"id":"handling-small-fit-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/3","message":"ac4 unconditionally requires small requests to remain undivided, although measured size does not guarantee that their content fits a model call. A single long document can measure XS by file/item counts while exceeding the selected model's input capacity. This conflicts with ac6's requirement to account for the whole oversized item and would reject the existing capacity-preserving fallback. Qualify ac4 to require undivided handling when the complete rendered input fits; otherwise permit partitioning with complete coverage and reported handling.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:164 — unconditional undivided handling for small requests","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:166 — whole-content handling for oversized items","src/analyze/measure.ts:82 — size thresholds count files and items rather than model input capacity","src/analyze/context/handling.ts:114 — admission can select partitioning independently of measured size","src/analyze/context/__tests__/handling-table.test.ts — XS input exceeding the local input limit requires partitioning","src/analyze/context/__tests__/partition-combine.test.ts — an admitted S request refused by the provider as oversized falls back to partitioning"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/2","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/5","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/6","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/14","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/15","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/16","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/17","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/18","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/3","/body/constraints/6","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:155-194 — serial child plans and terminal report materialization","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:248-266 — persistence and partial child-plan failures","design/analyze-context-builder.md:165-183 — lossless context and failure behavior","src/analyze/measure.ts","src/analyze/context/handling.ts","src/analyze/context/handling-parts.ts","src/analyze/context/handling-adapters.ts","src/analyze/context/dependency.ts","src/analyze/context/sections.ts","src/analyze/context/synthesizer.ts:150-245","src/analyze/completeness.ts","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts:340-390","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/aggregator.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/aggregate-types.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/docs/aggregate-report.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/docs/family-summarise.ts","src/analyze/explore/item-measure.ts","src/analyze/item-length.ts","src/analyze/explore/doc-constraint-enumerate.ts:235-285","src/analyze/explore/doc-decision-trace.ts:245-290","src/prompts/analyze/docs.aggregate.system.md","src/analyze/context/__tests__/handling-table.test.ts","src/analyze/context/__tests__/partition-combine.test.ts","src/analyze/context/__tests__/partition-sections.test.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/__tests__/aggregator-handling.test.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/__tests__/docs-aggregate-run.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Include acceptance fixtures where a conclusion requires evidence from different partitions or adjacent sections. Preserving independently produced findings alone does not demonstrate preservation of relationships across boundaries.","Exercise repeated combining with intermediate inputs exceeding capacity, retaining finding identities and citations through every level. Keep this distinct from s9's execution-budget policy and its already reported completeness ambiguity.","Tests and live model analyses were not executed; this read-only DEF assessment inspected relevant runtime contracts and test assertions."]},{"chunkId":"retrieval","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed against the live DEF, canonical artifact, upstream designs and relevant code/test contracts. Retrieval coverage and prerequisite ordering are broadly coherent. Two acceptance gaps require correction. No additional visual artifact is necessary for this epic-level capability.","findings":[{"id":"retrieval-stale-pointer-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/1","message":"Authoritative file retrieval does not define what happens when the indexed pointer is stale. Reading the recorded line range after an edit can successfully return unrelated text, so s1's generic failed-lookup reporting does not protect against this case. Define observable behavior for changed, missing or unreadable files and unverifiable pointers: establish that the content still corresponds to the indexed item, or report that item as uncovered without claiming complete coverage. Include acceptance cases for shifted line ranges and unavailable files; this need not expand scope into rebuilding the index.","evidenceReferences":["/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/23 — requires authoritative content at the indexed location","DEF.md:178 — s4/ac2 requires reading from the indexed pointer without a validity condition","src/analyze/item-length.ts:43-94 — existing measurement distinguishes changed, missing, unreadable and hash-unverified files","src/analyze/__tests__/item-length.test.ts:94-125 — shifted lines demonstrate that the recorded range can contain different text","DEF.md section 3 — changing index construction and freshness remains outside scope"]},{"id":"retrieval-sampling-completeness-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/4","message":"ac5 unconditionally requires a complete answer whenever removing a limit enlarges a result set. Such a request can also contain the Redis/etcd listing that ac6 explicitly requires to remain sampled and incomplete, or another failed source covered by s3/ac5. The flattened S004:FR001 also omits the sampling qualification present in the story's local functional requirement. Align these statements: require complete processing of available results while retaining sampled, failed or uncovered-source status in the answer, and reserve a complete-coverage claim for requests whose evidence supports it.","evidenceReferences":["/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/4 — unconditional complete-answer requirement","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/5 — samples must not be presented as complete","/body/stories/3/functionalRequirements/0 — explicitly qualifies sampled sources","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/19 — flattened requirement lacks that qualification","DEF.md:165 — s3/ac5 retains other findings while reporting failed parts as uncovered","src/daemon/db/drivers/redis.ts:166-191 — namespace discovery uses a bounded key sample"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/3","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/5","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/3","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/19","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/20","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/21","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/22","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/23","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-context-builder.md — lossless relevance window, caching and failure contracts","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:155-194 — serial partition execution and aggregation","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:248-266 — partial failures and dependency changes","src/analyze/item-length.ts","src/analyze/explore/item-measure.ts","src/analyze/__tests__/item-length.test.ts","src/analyze/explore/search-text.ts","src/analyze/explore/completeness-facts.ts:100-135","src/daemon/tools/builtins/search/grep.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/search/__tests__/grep-omitted.test.ts:245-280","src/analyze/explore/db-tables-list.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/data/discovery-objects.ts:30-110","src/analyze/runtimes/infra/_shared.ts:65-140","src/analyze/runtimes/docs/family-summarise.ts:150-180","src/analyze/docs-retrieval.ts:270-310","src/prompts/analyze/decompose.system.md — fixed-count examples and planning instructions","src/daemon/db/drivers/redis.ts — bounded namespace sampling","src/daemon/db/drivers/etcd.ts — sampled namespace discovery"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Use acceptance fixtures covering both analyzer paths and every family, including oversized content, per-file and total search limits, long lines, large files, and planner examples.","Retain regression coverage for bounded non-analyzer callers when adding uncapped search access. Exercise ripgrep and fallback behavior with explicit eligibility rules; their current exclusion and glob semantics differ.","Tests and live analyses were not executed; relevant source contracts and test assertions were inspected."]},{"chunkId":"answers","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The assigned requirements cover question-shaped answers, all six synthesizer families, legacy layouts, evidence grounding and trailing structural references. Two inconsistencies remain: s5 lacks prerequisites for exhaustive enumeration, and its unconditional completeness promise conflicts with explicitly supported incomplete evidence.","findings":[{"id":"answers-prerequisites-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/4","message":"s5 depends only on s1, but ac1 requires complete occurrence enumeration and ac2 removes answer-layout limits. s1 supplies reporting; measured sizing, partitioned handling and uncapped retrieval arrive through s2–s4. The declared dependency therefore permits accepting s5 while retrieval still omits occurrences or synthesis cannot handle them. It also contradicts the stakeholder's recorded order: reporting, sizing, handling, limit removal, then layouts. Declare the required predecessors, or separate question-shaped presentation from exhaustive enumeration and uncapping with explicit gates.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/4/dependsOn","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:194","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:200","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:101",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/17","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.code.system.md — export and artefact caps","src/prompts/analyze/docs.system.md — legacy layout caps"]},{"id":"answers-completeness-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/0","message":"ac1 and S005:FR001 promise a complete enumeration whenever the question asks for every occurrence, without qualifying the evidence available. This conflicts with s3/ac5, which delivers surviving findings while reporting failed parts, s4/ac6, which preserves incomplete Redis/etcd samples, and the non-goal deferring missing graph-edge repair. For example, an exhaustive caller question cannot establish complete occurrence coverage from an acknowledged incomplete call graph. Require enumeration of every established occurrence with its location, preserve uncovered or sampled-source disclosures, and permit a complete-coverage claim only when the evidence supports it. Apply the same qualification to the flattened requirement.","evidenceReferences":["/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/24","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:200","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:99","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:165","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:186","src/prompts/analyze/decompose.system.md — usage.example enumerates callers through CALLS edges","src/analyze/context/__tests__/partition-combine.test.ts — failed parts retain successful results and report uncovered work"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/4","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/4/localConstraints/0","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/4","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/5","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/24","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/25","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/26","/body/constraints/4","/body/constraints/5","/body/constraints/6","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json — completed substantive feedback","CLAUDE.md — accuracy and trailing structural-reference conventions","design/analyze-context-builder.md","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — partitioned plans, aggregation and partial completeness","site/analyze.html — exploration-grounded claims","src/analyze/context/driver.ts — synthesizer dispatch and freeform fallback","src/analyze/context/synthesizer.ts — single and partitioned answer composition","src/analyze/explore/types.ts — supported exploration catalog","src/prompts/analyze/decompose.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.code.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.docs.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.adherence.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.capability.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.data.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.infra.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/code.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/docs.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/data.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/infra.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/generic.system.md","src/analyze/context/__tests__/partition-combine.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["At detailed design, use an acceptance matrix spanning the six synthesizers and legacy fallbacks, with results exceeding former caps, every supported exploration output, irrelevant sections left empty, and enumeration preserved across partition boundaries. Keep literal-search routing outside s5 as the non-goals require.","No authored or generated visual accompanies the assigned requirements; their presentation and dependency rules are assessable in prose, so no additional diagram is necessary at DEF stage."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"passed","summary":"Completed whole-artifact consistency inspection and read all seven accepted substantive assessments. All 126 inventory units have inspection declarations, with no outstanding mandatory verification limitations. Live Markdown and canonical artifact match the reviewed baseline; canonical requirement statements and story acceptance criteria agree across representations. Declared dependencies are acyclic. The s7 exceptions are explicitly closed by s3 and s8. Existing feedback already captures the dependency gaps, budget/upstream conflicts, completeness contradictions and citation defect; no additional distinct defect was demonstrated. This chunk's passed status does not clear those earlier findings. No additional visual artifact is necessary at DEF stage.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","Checkpoint attempt 1: completedChunks scope, broad, reporting, sizing, handling, retrieval and answers; inventory and plan coverage","DEF.md:26-80 — flattened requirements and accepted s7 exceptions","DEF.md:114-269 — all nine stories, acceptance criteria and prerequisites","DEF.md:271-297 — citations and open question","design/analyze-context-builder.md — context ownership, lossless sizing and failure contracts","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — recursive contracts, validation, XL child plans, persistence and partial failures","design/analyze-framework.md:35-100 — five size policies, intent and citation contracts","design/analyze-framework-code.md:1-95 — module discovery and functional-surface contracts","CLAUDE.md:9-12,117-147 — accuracy, sequential model calls, IPC ownership and prompt conventions","src/analyze/completeness.ts:35-115 — unknown totals and completeness basis","src/analyze/context/handling.ts:55-145 — capacity admission independent of measured size","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/source-modules.ts:1-155 — directory-module identity and ownership"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Retain the existing prerequisite findings scope-order-01, answers-prerequisites-01 and sizing-prerequisites-01 when reconciling rollout order. s9's docs completion criterion also relies on closing s7's oversized-combination exception through s3.","Resolve scope-budget-02 and sizing-budget-completeness-02 together against the upstream XL child-plan policy; sizing-aggregate-policy-03 and sizing-timing-acceptance-04 identify separate acceptance gaps.","Preserve the distinctions identified by reporting-unknown-total-01, handling-small-fit-01, retrieval-stale-pointer-01, retrieval-sampling-completeness-02 and answers-completeness-02: processing all available evidence does not establish complete source coverage.","Keep scope-citation-03 and the existing advice about s8/s9 requirement identifiers and historical baseline citations visible during correction. No tests, live analyses or timing benchmarks were executed; these are optional execution activities for this DEF review."]}],"limitations":[],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIden