d","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":13,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Assessed all assigned scope selectors, the live DEF, canonical artifact, cited evidence available in the repository, and applicable upstream designs. Three scope and traceability defects require correction. No authored/generated visual is present or necessary to assess this epic-level capability definition.","findings":[{"id":"scope-order-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/4/dependsOn","message":"Story s5 removes answer-layout limits but depends only on s1, allowing it to run before measured sizing and complete handling exist. This contradicts FR004 and the explicit non-goal prohibiting removal of any limit before the analyzer can handle what it admits. Make layout-limit removal depend on the relevant sizing/handling capabilities, or separate layout selection from uncapping with an explicit prerequisite.","evidenceReferences":["DEF.md:32 — FR004 prohibits removing limits before handling exists","DEF.md:101 — non-goal requires completeness, measurement and handling before limit removal","DEF.md:194-201 — s5 depends only on s1 and removes all layout finding limits",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/4"]},{"id":"scope-budget-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8","message":"Story s9 introduces aggregate child-task limits and an execution budget without defining how coverage survives reaching them. It also prohibits large child plans for L/XL requests, whereas the applicable upstream design explicitly uses L-sized child plans to cover XL partitions. The DEF simultaneously requires processing every part with no findings lost and excludes reducing time/model cost. Specify the intended replacement depth policy and whether budget exhaustion causes incomplete failure, resumable continuation, or coverage-preserving replanning; distinguish that behavior from successful complete analysis.","evidenceReferences":["DEF.md:89 — reducing time/model usage is a non-goal","DEF.md:108-109 — k1 and k2 require accuracy and lossless inclusion","DEF.md:161-167 — s3 requires complete processing and combination","DEF.md:265-269 — s9 introduces shallow child plans, task limits and execution budgets","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:155-194 — XL partitions normally spawn L child plans","design/analyze-framework.md:42-46 — five-bucket depth and coverage policy"]},{"id":"scope-citation-03","severity":"MED","location":"/citations/20/id","message":"Citation id c21 is duplicated: index 18 identifies the historical unfocused-request failure, while index 20 identifies the Redis/etcd sampling decision. Consequently, the assumption and s6/s7 references to c21 cannot resolve uniquely and may select unrelated evidence. Give the sampling decision a distinct id and update its references while preserving the failure evidence identity.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/18",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/20",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/assumptions/3/source","DEF.md:215,232,291,293 — c21 references and conflicting definitions"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/flavor","/body/problem","/body/nonGoals","/body/assumptions","/body/constraints","/body/stories","/body/openQuestions","/body/functionalDefinition","document:line:26","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/3","/body/constraints/4","/body/constraints/5","/body/constraints/6","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/citations/9","/citations/10","/citations/11","/citations/12","/citations/13","/citations/14","/citations/15","/citations/16","/citations/17","/citations/18","/citations/19","/citations/20","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/