etain the explicit boundaries for graph repair, index freshness, live-store sampling and general-purpose tool callers when refining acceptance criteria. Historical external logs and live-run observations were assessed as recorded evidence; replaying those measurements is optional for this scope review."]},{"chunkId":"broad","status":"passed","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the live DEF, canonical requirements, upstream designs and relevant runtime/test sources. The s6–s8 boundaries are feasible: context entry precedes lifecycle execution, directory-module support completes the code-family path, and s3 explicitly closes the accepted docs aggregation exception. No blocking design defect was demonstrated. No authored or generated visual is attached to this DEF; its epic-level interactions and ownership requirements are adequately expressed in prose.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/5","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/6","/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/7","/body/stories/7/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/7/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/7/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/7/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/7/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/6","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/27","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/28","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/29","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/30","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/31","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","DEF.md sections 6.6–6.8 — context entry, lifecycle, module discovery and compatibility acceptance","DEF.md section 2, S007:FR003 — docs aggregation exception and code-family dependency","DEF.md section 6.3, ac7 — closure of the docs aggregation exception","design/analyze-context-builder.md:69-183 — bundle ownership, broad context, caching and distinct failure causes","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:63-83,155-194,248-266 — nested report materialization, serial execution, persistence and partial failures","design/analyze-framework-code.md:5-20,39-69 — code scopes, discovery and functional-surface expectations","src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1590-1675 — unfocused run-mode entry and cause-specific pipeline failures","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:153-207,254-329 — terminal failures, stored-result retrieval and source-hinted entry","src/analyze/orchestrator/persistence.ts:103-136 — abandoned-run terminal records","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts:340-390 — nested execution and child report materialization","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/source-modules.ts — directory identity, stored-module ownership, path normalization and invalid values","src/analyze/runtimes/code/discovery-modules.ts — shared module definition and discovery output","src/analyze/runtimes/code/structure-module-tree.ts — module nodes, file ownership and import-edge contracts","src/analyze/runtimes/code/surface-functional.ts — directory and entity-id inputs, recursive surface and explicit refusals","src/analyze/runtimes/code/__tests__/module-directories.test.ts:128-185,363-535 — discovery, ownership, compatibility and invalid-module scenarios","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/hinted-branch.test.ts:68-100 — focused and unfocused source-hinted requests","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/shaper-causes.test.ts:56 — cause-specific failures and recorded terminal output","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/orchestrator.test.ts:489-540 — completed-run replay assertions","src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-run-abandoned.test.ts — observable abandonment and terminal-record preservation scenarios","src/indexer/parser/go.ts:376-391 — imported-module entities use an empty repository/file","src/indexer/parser/python.ts:223-235 — imported-module entities use an empty repository/file"],"limitations":[],"advice":["When refining acceptance fixtures, explicitly cover mixed-language directories, source only in descendants, overlapping stored modules, and relative versus absolute module values. The current shared runtime supplies concrete identity and ownership rules that can anchor those fixtures.","Keep completion evidence distinct from report existence: verify nested results reach the report and inspect functional-surface task statuses, as s7/ac2 and s8/ac5 require.","Tests and live analyses were not executed; this read-only DEF assessment inspected their source contracts and assertions."]},{"chunkId":"reporting","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned reporting selectors were assessed. Failure distinction, partial-read reporting, evidence preservation and prohibition of silent answer fallback are coherent and feasible on both paths. One acceptance criterion conflicts with retained sampling and unknown-total results. No additional visual artifact is necessary for this epic-level capability.","findings":[{"id":"reporting-unknown-total-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/0","message":"ac1 requires every incomplete lookup or analysis step to report how many results exist, without allowing an unknown total. This cannot be satisfied for unreadable sources, searches stopped before enumeration finishes, or the Redis/etcd samples explicitly retained by s4/ac6 without scanning every key. It also conflicts with the current result contract, which correctly permits total: null. Require exact totals when established; otherwise require an explicit unknown total and its reason, alongside the returned count and completeness basis. This makes s1 independently acceptable before limits are removed and avoids encouraging fabricated counts or prohibited full scans.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:126 — unconditional total requirement","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:186 — sampled Redis/etcd listings remain incomplete and must not scan every key","src/analyze/completeness.ts:61-70 — Completeness.total explicitly permits null","src/analyze/explore/completeness-facts.ts:101-117 — stopped text searches cannot establish the total","src/analyze/explore/__tests__/completeness-all-lookups.test.ts:387,431 — document and stopped-search fixtures assert unknown totals"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/5","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/0","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/7","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/8","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/9","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/10","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/11","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/6","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-context-builder.md — bundle ownership, lossless context and failure surfaces","design/analyze-framework.md:245-270 — task failures, absent producers and aggregation provenance","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:248-266 — resumability and partial child-plan failure","site/analyze.html:38-61 — analyzer entry points and exploration-grounded claims","src/analyze/completeness.ts — result contracts, derived answer reports and incomplete-source reasons","src/analyze/explore/completeness-facts.ts — graph-relative completeness, exclusion rules and unknown totals","src/analyze/explore/answer-report.ts — failed, unsupported and missing-record propagation","src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1735-1855 — exploration preservation and terminal synthesis failures","src/analyze/context/synthesizer.ts — evidence-only synthesis and typed answer failures","src/analyze/context/answer-step-error.ts — retained lookup results, upstream inputs and failure causes","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts:264-334 — task failure and completeness-record enforcement","src/daemon/steps/analyze-step/phases/bundle.ts — independently derived reports and terminal invalid-answer evidence","src/analyze/runtimes/data/discovery-objects.ts — driver listing cuts and unknown totals","src/analyze/__tests__/completeness.test.ts — complete-empty, incomplete, failed and partly-read contract assertions","src/analyze/explore/__tests__/completeness-all-lookups.test.ts — lookup coverage and known/unknown count assertions","src/daemon/steps/__tests__/analyze-step-bundle-report.test.ts — derived report and forged-completeness rejection assertions","src/daemon/steps/__tests__/analyze-step-answer-prompt-missing.test.ts — plan/narrow failure evidence preservation","src/analyze/context/__tests__/answer-failure-mapping.test.ts — daemon and plan-tree failure payload preservation","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.code.system.md — failed lookup diagnostics and freeform completeness basis","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.adherence.system.md — incomplete text evidence diagnostics","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.data.system.md — failed versus complete-empty listings"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Make graph-relative completeness and sampled-source incompleteness explicit fixtures for s1/ac5, retaining the DEF's graph-repair non-goal.","Tests and live analyses were not executed; this read-only DEF assessment inspected relevant contracts and test assertions."]},{"chunkId":"sizing","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Measured sizing covers both paths, caller hints, reporting and conservative unknown-size fallback. Story s9 lacks prerequisites and leaves bounded execution, aggregate limits and timing acceptance insufficiently defined.","findings":[{"id":"sizing-prerequisites-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8","message":"Story s9 has no dependsOn declaration although its criteria require measured sizes supplied by s2 and an executable broad-analysis path supplied by s7. The tracked ordering therefore permits s9 before its prerequisites. Declare those dependencies and identify any complete-handling prerequisite needed for its end-to-end docs criterion.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8 — no dependsOn field","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:139 — s2 prerequisites","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:225 — s7 provides broad execution","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:167 — s3 closes oversized docs aggregation"]},{"id":"sizing-budget-completeness-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","message":"Reporting that an execution budget was reached does not define what happens to unfinished coverage, completed findings or the final report. A bounded run can satisfy ac4 while abandoning work required by s3 and k2. Define the observable terminal outcome, retained findings and uncovered work, and whether continuation or coverage-preserving replanning completes the request. Distinguish budget exhaustion from successful complete analysis. Also reconcile ac1's prohibition on large child plans with the upstream XL policy that explicitly uses L-sized children; measured child sizes must not be relabelled merely to fit a budget.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:265-268","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:161-167 — whole-request handling and lossless combination",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/constraints/0",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/constraints/1",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/constraints/2","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — XL → planner-template tasks and Failure surface","src/analyze/planner/recursive.ts:158 — child size is measured independently"]},{"id":"sizing-aggregate-policy-03","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/2","message":"The aggregate rejection criterion refers to a total and what the request's size allows, but neither the counted resource nor the governing aggregate policy is identified. Existing task-count bands apply separately to each plan, and the existing root depth ceiling does not bound the sum of child tasks. Specify what is totalled, which descendants and root work count, and which size-based policy governs rejection and execution. Cover XS explicitly or state that its existing policy is retained; ac1 and ac2 currently cover only four of the five supported sizes.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:265-268","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — invariant 13 applies to each individual plan","design/analyze-framework.md:42-46 — five supported size policies","src/analyze/planner/scope-band.ts — per-plan task-count bands","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:159 — taskCountFailure checks plan.tasks.length","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:209 — separate root-scope depth ceiling"]},{"id":"sizing-timing-acceptance-04","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","message":"“Within a stated time” supplies no acceptance threshold or rule for establishing one before execution. Any completed run can pass by stating a time above its observed duration, so this does not test the story's promised reasonable completion time. Identify the broad docs request and repository fixture or revision, establish the time target and relevant execution conditions before the run, and define the measured interval. Retain the required depth and task-count records alongside that result.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:261 — reasonable completion time is the stated user value","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:269 — no timing threshold, request fixture or execution conditions"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/8","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/1","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/12","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/13","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-plan-builder.md","design/analyze-framework.md — scope policies and root depth ceiling","design/analyze-context-builder.md — Sizing","docs/daemon.md — How a request's size is measured","src/analyze/classifier/driver.ts — unsized classifier contract","src/analyze/measure.ts — count mapping, hints, unknown fallback and sampled sources","src/mcp/server.ts — structured request and sizeHint schema","src/daemon/steps/analyze-step/phases/start.ts — measurement before planning","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts — measurement and planner handoff","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts — measured-size stamping and depth ceiling","src/analyze/planner/recursive.ts — nested planning and child measurement","src/analyze/planner/scope-band.ts","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts — per-plan count validation","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts — serial execution and task records","src/analyze/__tests__/measure.test.ts — sizing boundaries and monotonicity","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/run-measure.test.ts — measured-size planner integration"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Link s9 explicitly to the functional requirements it extends and the constraints its acceptance criteria operationalize.","Preserve the documented Redis/etcd exception: report sampling and unknown measurements, use XL conservatively, and avoid a full key scan.","No authored or generated visual is attached to these assigned capabilities; the DEF-level sizing requirements can be assessed in prose. Tests and live timing runs were not executed during this read-only design review."]},{"chunkId":"handling","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed. Partition coverage, retained findings, partial failures, sequential model calls and closure of the docs aggregation exception are coherent at DEF level. One acceptance criterion incorrectly prohibits partitioning small requests whose content exceeds model capacity. No additional visual artifact is necessary for this capability at this stage.","findings":[{"id":"handling-small-fit-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/3","message":"ac4 unconditionally requires small requests to remain undivided, although measured size does not guarantee that their content fits a model call. A single long document can measure XS by file/item counts while exceeding the selected model's input capacity. This conflicts with ac6's requirement to account for the whole oversized item and would reject the existing capacity-preserving fallback. Qualify ac4 to require undivided handling when the complete rendered input fits; otherwise permit partitioning with complete coverage and reported handling.","evidenceReferences":["docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:164 — unconditional undivided handling for small requests","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:166 — whole-content handling for oversized items","src/analyze/measure.ts:82 — size thresholds count files and items rather than model input capacity","src/analyze/context/handling.ts:114 — admission can select partitioning independently of measured size","src/analyze/context/__tests__/handling-table.test.ts — XS input exceeding the local input limit requires partitioning","src/analyze/context/__tests__/partition-combine.test.ts — an admitted S request refused by the provider as oversized falls back to partitioning"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/2","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/5","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/6","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/14","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/15","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/16","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/17","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/18","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/3","/body/constraints/6","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:155-194 — serial child plans and terminal report materialization","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:248-266 — persistence and partial child-plan failures","design/analyze-context-builder.md:165-183 — lossless context and failure behavior","src/analyze/measure.ts","src/analyze/context/handling.ts","src/analyze/context/handling-parts.ts","src/analyze/context/handling-adapters.ts","src/analyze/context/dependency.ts","src/analyze/context/sections.ts","src/analyze/context/synthesizer.ts:150-245","src/analyze/completeness.ts","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts:340-390","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/aggregator.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/aggregate-types.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/docs/aggregate-report.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/docs/family-summarise.ts","src/analyze/explore/item-measure.ts","src/analyze/item-length.ts","src/analyze/explore/doc-constraint-enumerate.ts:235-285","src/analyze/explore/doc-decision-trace.ts:245-290","src/prompts/analyze/docs.aggregate.system.md","src/analyze/context/__tests__/handling-table.test.ts","src/analyze/context/__tests__/partition-combine.test.ts","src/analyze/context/__tests__/partition-sections.test.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/__tests__/aggregator-handling.test.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/__tests__/docs-aggregate-run.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Include acceptance fixtures where a conclusion requires evidence from different partitions or adjacent sections. Preserving independently produced findings alone does not demonstrate preservation of relationships across boundaries.","Exercise repeated combining with intermediate inputs exceeding capacity, retaining finding identities and citations through every level. Keep this distinct from s9's execution-budget policy and its already reported completeness ambiguity.","Tests and live model analyses were not executed; this read-only DEF assessment inspected relevant runtime contracts and test assertions."]},{"chunkId":"retrieval","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed against the live DEF, canonical artifact, upstream designs and relevant code/test contracts. Retrieval coverage and prerequisite ordering are broadly coherent. Two acceptance gaps require correction. No additional visual artifact is necessary for this epic-level capability.","findings":[{"id":"retrieval-stale-pointer-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/1","message":"Authoritative file retrieval does not define what happens when the indexed pointer is stale. Reading the recorded line range after an edit can successfully return unrelated text, so s1's generic failed-lookup reporting does not protect against this case. Define observable behavior for changed, missing or unreadable files and unverifiable pointers: establish that the content still corresponds to the indexed item, or report that item as uncovered without claiming complete coverage. Include acceptance cases for shifted line ranges and unavailable files; this need not expand scope into rebuilding the index.","evidenceReferences":["/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/23 — requires authoritative content at the indexed location","DEF.md:178 — s4/ac2 requires reading from the indexed pointer without a validity condition","src/analyze/item-length.ts:43-94 — existing measurement distinguishes changed, missing, unreadable and hash-unverified files","src/analyze/__tests__/item-length.test.ts:94-125 — shifted lines demonstrate that the recorded range can contain different text","DEF.md section 3 — changing index construction and freshness remains outside scope"]},{"id":"retrieval-sampling-completeness-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/4","message":"ac5 unconditionally requires a complete answer whenever removing a limit enlarges a result set. Such a request can also contain the Redis/etcd listing that ac6 explicitly requires to remain sampled and incomplete, or another failed source covered by s3/ac5. The flattened S004:FR001 also omits the sampling qualification present in the story's local functional requirement. Align these statements: require complete processing of available results while retaining sampled, failed or uncovered-source status in the answer, and reserve a complete-coverage claim for requests whose evidence supports it.","evidenceReferences":["/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/4 — unconditional complete-answer requirement","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/5 — samples must not be presented as complete","/body/stories/3/functionalRequirements/0 — explicitly qualifies sampled sources","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/19 — flattened requirement lacks that qualification","DEF.md:165 — s3/ac5 retains other findings while reporting failed parts as uncovered","src/daemon/db/drivers/redis.ts:166-191 — namespace discovery uses a bounded key sample"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/3","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/5","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/3","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/19","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/20","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/21","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/22","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/23","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-context-builder.md — lossless relevance window, caching and failure contracts","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:155-194 — serial partition execution and aggregation","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:248-266 — partial failures and dependency changes","src/analyze/item-length.ts","src/analyze/explore/item-measure.ts","src/analyze/__tests__/item-length.test.ts","src/analyze/explore/search-text.ts","src/analyze/explore/completeness-facts.ts:100-135","src/daemon/tools/builtins/search/grep.ts","src/daemon/tools/builtins/search/__tests__/grep-omitted.test.ts:245-280","src/analyze/explore/db-tables-list.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/data/discovery-objects.ts:30-110","src/analyze/runtimes/infra/_shared.ts:65-140","src/analyze/runtimes/docs/family-summarise.ts:150-180","src/analyze/docs-retrieval.ts:270-310","src/prompts/analyze/decompose.system.md — fixed-count examples and planning instructions","src/daemon/db/drivers/redis.ts — bounded namespace sampling","src/daemon/db/drivers/etcd.ts — sampled namespace discovery"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Use acceptance fixtures covering both analyzer paths and every family, including oversized content, per-file and total search limits, long lines, large files, and planner examples.","Retain regression coverage for bounded non-analyzer callers when adding uncapped search access. Exercise ripgrep and fallback behavior with explicit eligibility rules; their current exclusion and glob semantics differ.","Tests and live analyses were not executed; relevant source contracts and test assertions were inspected."]},{"chunkId":"answers","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The assigned requirements cover question-shaped answers, all six synthesizer families, legacy layouts, evidence grounding and trailing structural references. Two inconsistencies remain: s5 lacks prerequisites for exhaustive enumeration, and its unconditional completeness promise conflicts with explicitly supported incomplete evidence.","findings":[{"id":"answers-prerequisites-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/4","message":"s5 depends only on s1, but ac1 requires complete occurrence enumeration and ac2 removes answer-layout limits. s1 supplies reporting; measured sizing, partitioned handling and uncapped retrieval arrive through s2–s4. The declared dependency therefore permits accepting s5 while retrieval still omits occurrences or synthesis cannot handle them. It also contradicts the stakeholder's recorded order: reporting, sizing, handling, limit removal, then layouts. Declare the required predecessors, or separate question-shaped presentation from exhaustive enumeration and uncapping with explicit gates.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/4/dependsOn","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:194","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:200","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:101",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/17","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.code.system.md — export and artefact caps","src/prompts/analyze/docs.system.md — legacy layout caps"]},{"id":"answers-completeness-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/0","message":"ac1 and S005:FR001 promise a complete enumeration whenever the question asks for every occurrence, without qualifying the evidence available. This conflicts with s3/ac5, which delivers surviving findings while reporting failed parts, s4/ac6, which preserves incomplete Redis/etcd samples, and the non-goal deferring missing graph-edge repair. For example, an exhaustive caller question cannot establish complete occurrence coverage from an acknowledged incomplete call graph. Require enumeration of every established occurrence with its location, preserve uncovered or sampled-source disclosures, and permit a complete-coverage claim only when the evidence supports it. Apply the same qualification to the flattened requirement.","evidenceReferences":["/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/24","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:200","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:99","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:165","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:186","src/prompts/analyze/decompose.system.md — usage.example enumerates callers through CALLS edges","src/analyze/context/__tests__/partition-combine.test.ts — failed parts retain successful results and report uncovered work"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/4","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/4/localConstraints/0","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/4","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/5","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/24","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/25","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/26","/body/constraints/4","/body/constraints/5","/body/constraints/6","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json — completed substantive feedback","CLAUDE.md — accuracy and trailing structural-reference conventions","design/analyze-context-builder.md","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — partitioned plans, aggregation and partial completeness","site/analyze.html — exploration-grounded claims","src/analyze/context/driver.ts — synthesizer dispatch and freeform fallback","src/analyze/context/synthesizer.ts — single and partitioned answer composition","src/analyze/explore/types.ts — supported exploration catalog","src/prompts/analyze/decompose.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.code.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.docs.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.adherence.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.capability.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.data.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.infra.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/code.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/docs.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/data.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/infra.system.md","src/prompts/analyze/generic.system.md","src/analyze/context/__tests__/partition-combine.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["At detailed design, use an acceptance matrix spanning the six synthesizers and legacy fallbacks, with results exceeding former caps, every supported exploration output, irrelevant sections left empty, and enumeration preserved across partition boundaries. Keep literal-search routing outside s5 as the non-goals require.","No authored or generated visual accompanies the assigned requirements; their presentation and dependency rules are assessable in prose, so no additional diagram is necessary at DEF stage."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"passed","summary":"Completed whole-artifact consistency inspection and read all seven accepted substantive assessments. All 126 inventory units have inspection declarations, with no outstanding mandatory verification limitations. Live Markdown and canonical artifact match the reviewed baseline; canonical requirement statements and story acceptance criteria agree across representations. Declared dependencies are acyclic. The s7 exceptions are explicitly closed by s3 and s8. Existing feedback already captures the dependency gaps, budget/upstream conflicts, completeness contradictions and citation defect; no additional distinct defect was demonstrated. This chunk's passed status does not clear those earlier findings. No additional visual artifact is necessary at DEF stage.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","Checkpoint attempt 1: completedChunks scope, broad, reporting, sizing, handling, retrieval and answers; inventory and plan coverage","DEF.md:26-80 — flattened requirements and accepted s7 exceptions","DEF.md:114-269 — all nine stories, acceptance criteria and prerequisites","DEF.md:271-297 — citations and open question","design/analyze-context-builder.md — context ownership, lossless sizing and failure contracts","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — recursive contracts, validation, XL child plans, persistence and partial failures","design/analyze-framework.md:35-100 — five size policies, intent and citation contracts","design/analyze-framework-code.md:1-95 — module discovery and functional-surface contracts","CLAUDE.md:9-12,117-147 — accuracy, sequential model calls, IPC ownership and prompt conventions","src/analyze/completeness.ts:35-115 — unknown totals and completeness basis","src/analyze/context/handling.ts:55-145 — capacity admission independent of measured size","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/source-modules.ts:1-155 — directory-module identity and ownership"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Retain the existing prerequisite findings scope-order-01, answers-prerequisites-01 and sizing-prerequisites-01 when reconciling rollout order. s9's docs completion criterion also relies on closing s7's oversized-combination exception through s3.","Resolve scope-budget-02 and sizing-budget-completeness-02 together against the upstream XL child-plan policy; sizing-aggregate-policy-03 and sizing-timing-acceptance-04 identify separate acceptance gaps.","Preserve the distinctions identified by reporting-unknown-total-01, handling-small-fit-01, retrieval-stale-pointer-01, retrieval-sampling-completeness-02 and answers-completeness-02: processing all available evidence does not establish complete source coverage.","Keep scope-citation-03 and the existing advice about s8/s9 requirement identifiers and historical baseline citations visible during correction. No tests, live analyses or timing benchmarks were executed; these are optional execution activities for this DEF review."]}],"limitations":[],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"226b6d13e625dbad5c167f030f9a178a69b8a9897d5be713b001c7bd56d2be36"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-13T12:18:53.688Z","publication":{"reviewId":"analyzer-def-s9-r1","attempt":1,"state":"complete","artifactHistoryEntryId":"8bd4408dfcc550b3b5e0eecd15d98464c63216e2c7e1cc04caa58daad4a968e7","reportReference":"8bd4408dfcc550b3b5e0eecd15d98464c63216e2c7e1cc04caa58daad4a968e7","canonicalBefore":"f2928034605ac09581b91249bb1daf2035a632ec0e1017b8452fab40d448cc9d","canonicalAfter":"1028ec1c39ed5710c0c023b52278210072f86ee17e42da57539d3b7ef922beb3"},"submitted":{"artifactPath":"/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","attempt":1},"actionId":"start-1","operation":"start","acceptedAt":"2026-11-13T12:03:11.039Z","resourceGuard":{"daemonInstance":"b361638a-b6bf-42ea-8be7-8d610ff4bbeb","openLeases":[]}},{"number":2,"status":"invalidated","preparationKind":"impact","baseline":{"subjectFingerprints":{"canonical":"c76fb8a24c3c4e0abc02d65b5c0ebb7fc781b29707f72f9c8e34e937f376fed0","document":"f51eb32196b0c45ce84bcaf8c05bb42a72fe6dd71ec6325e2be27da4446999e7"},"contentIdentity":"91358dd682d748eaa8995437fe233cce3cd5805438af01638b10fa0f01840c05","reviewedContent":{"canonical":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"workflow\": \"define\",\n    \"runId\": \"wf-1791308718624-m82cgl\",\n    \"repoPath\": \"/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-06T17:47:38.720Z\",\n    \"attribution\": {\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"(client)\",\n          \"tier\": \"core\",\n          \"runner\": \"cli-claude\",\n          \"model\": \"client\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"elapsedMs\": 140094,\n    \"repoIndexedAt\": null,\n    \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n    \"epicHash\": \"b9d5c5c40df5a574\",\n    \"epicSlug\": \"make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right\",\n    \"authoredBy\": \"controller\",\n    \"questionResolutions\": {\n      \"qc698b1fc\": {\n        \"question\": \"The per-turn reminder that tells agents to use the analyzer first is a hook script on the user's machine (~/.claude/hooks/insrc-steering-reminder.sh) and no source for it was found in this repository. Where is it maintained and installed from, so that Story s5 can change it?\",\n        \"status\": \"resolved\",\n        \"choice\": \"Retire the hook, use the steering block\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The user confirmed on 2026-10-07 that the script is a legacy artifact on one machine and is absent from other machines where insrc is installed. It is registered only in that machine's ~/.claude/settings.json (UserPromptSubmit), dated 2026-07-24, and this repository never shipped it. Story s5 changes the steering block, which is the only guidance insrc installs; the per-turn reminder is not a product surface.\",\n        \"resolvedAt\": \"2026-10-06T18:55:19.772Z\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"epicCreatedAt\": \"2026-10-06T17:47:38.720Z\",\n    \"envelope\": {\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"references\": [],\n      \"attachments\": []\n    },\n    \"lifecycle\": {\n      \"status\": \"draft\",\n      \"revision\": {\n        \"number\": 1,\n        \"contentHash\": \"4937fec2968bff4d603b342e2767cfcd8ea0852bc53a05da9c2ce2ddac2f6985\",\n        \"at\": \"2026-11-12T01:23:43.549Z\",\n        \"by\": {\n          \"id\": \"insrc:system\",\n          \"kind\": \"system\",\n          \"properties\": {}\n        }\n      },\n      \"approval\": {\n        \"revision\": 0,\n        \"by\": {\n          \"id\": \"legacy:unknown\",\n          \"kind\": \"person\",\n          \"properties\": {}\n        },\n        \"at\": \"2026-10-09T12:04:22.289Z\",\n        \"override\": {\n          \"reason\": \"User-approved override, 2026-10-09 (the user chose in chat: approve the Define by override, with no fresh daemon review). The Define's approval was cleared by an in-place edit of one sentence (commit 366c359c): criterion ac3 of Story s8 said 'a repository whose graph does hold module entities, as for a language whose parser emits them'; it now says that no parser stores a module entity for a repository's own directories today and that a graph written by other means may hold them. Nothing else in the Define changed. The edit records the stakeholder's decision of 2026-10-09 on Story s8's design. No fresh review by the daemon was run on the amended text.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"signoffs\": [],\n      \"review\": {\n        \"revision\": 1,\n        \"reviewer\": {\n          \"id\": \"agent:design-review-daemon\",\n          \"kind\": \"agent\",\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"party\": \"daemon\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"party\": \"daemon\",\n        \"verdict\": \"block\",\n        \"counts\": {\n          \"HIGH\": 0,\n          \"MED\": 13,\n          \"LOW\": 0\n        },\n        \"at\": \"2026-11-13T12:18:53.688Z\",\n        \"report\": {\n          \"entityId\": \"DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574\",\n          \"type\": \"change-log-entry\",\n          \"relation\": \"reviews\",\n          \"fragment\": \"8bd4408dfcc550b3b5e0eecd15d98464c63216e2c7e1cc04caa58daad4a968e7\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"revision\": 1,\n    \"tracker\": {\n      \"adapter\": \"github\",\n      \"epicStatus\": \"open\",\n      \"storyStatus\": {},\n      \"lastSyncedAt\": \"2026-11-13T06:21:54.734Z\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"body\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"prose\": \"An analysis that silently leaves results out cannot be trusted, and today the analyzer does exactly that: every lookup it makes stops at a fixed number of results and reports as if it had seen everything. This Epic first makes every result and answer say honestly whether it is complete, then makes the analyzer measure how large a question really is and handle each size by a method that covers all of it, and only then removes the limits, so that at no point is a limit taken away before the analyzer can handle what it lets through. It also gives answers a shape that fits what was asked.\",\n      \"audience\": \"product\"\n    },\n    \"flavor\": \"enhancement\",\n    \"problem\": \"The analyzer's findings are incomplete in a way neither the analyzer nor its reader can see. Each of its lookups returns at most a fixed number of results, chosen once and unrelated to the size of the question, and the rest are dropped without the answer saying so; some lookups that fail outright read the same as ones that found nothing. The same question therefore gets a correct answer on a small area of a codebase and a wrong one on a large area, with nothing to tell them apart, which contradicts the framework's own stated rule that nothing relevant is cut. How large a request is gets decided up front from its wording and the overall size of the repository, not from what the question actually touches, and when the analyzer is called through the tools coding agents use it is not decided at all and a middle size is assumed; that size sets how many steps are planned and how much an answer may report, and plays no part in how a large result is dealt with. The answer is then written to one of six fixed layouts, chosen by the kind of source or check and not by the kind of question, each of which suits one sort of answer, such as a structural overview, and each of which itself limits how much may be reported. Beneath all of this, a request that asks no specific question cannot be analysed at all: the analyzer builds no context for it and reports the model as unavailable although the model was never asked, and nothing shows that a broad analysis has run through to a final report.\",\n    \"nonGoals\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Reducing what an analysis costs in time or model usage.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The project rule puts accuracy first and cost last; a complete answer may take longer and that is accepted.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Routing every codebase question through the analyzer.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The stakeholder decided a simple text search stays a plain search; only questions about relationships or meaning need analysis.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Changing what the code index contains or how it is built.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The problem is results being dropped after they are found, not what is indexed; index freshness for files created in a session is a separate matter. The index is a pointer to an item: where an item's content matters to an answer, the analyzer reads the item from its file, which changes nothing in the index.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Removing limits that protect a model's input from a single oversized item, without a replacement.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"A very large item must still be read in full by some means; the Epic requires that it be handled in full, not that the protection simply vanish.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Changing the limits of the general-purpose search tools for callers other than the analyzer.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Other agents and tools call those primitives with their own expectations; the Epic concerns what the analyzer receives from them.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Guidance to coding agents on when to use their own search tools and when to use the analyzer.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The stakeholder decided this is steering text only and it was applied by hand on 2026-10-07 (commit 83a1cc0); nothing about it is built or enforced in this Epic.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Repairing the code graph's missing cross-file import and call edges.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Tracked separately as ISSUE-12f70133491114c9, to be taken up after this Epic; until then a relationship lookup can be incomplete for reasons this Epic does not address, and its results must say only what this Epic can establish about completeness.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Removing a limit before the analyzer can state completeness, measure a request and handle a large result.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The stakeholder chose an order in which no limit is taken away until what it lets through can be handled; the stories depend on one another accordingly.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"assumptions\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Every place the analyzer drops results can be found by reading its recipes, runtimes, prompts and the search primitives it calls.\",\n        \"confidence\": \"med\",\n        \"source\": \"c1\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"The number of results a request will touch can be counted before the request is run in full; today only the size of the whole repository is counted.\",\n        \"confidence\": \"med\",\n        \"source\": \"c2\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"A result set too large to reason over at once can be divided, reasoned over part by part, and combined without losing findings, building on the way the framework already runs a large plan as child plans whose results an aggregator combines.\",\n        \"confidence\": \"med\",\n        \"source\": \"c10\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"The stages of a broad analysis that lie beyond building the context (planning, running the plan, combining the results) work or can be corrected within Story s7; no completed run on record shows this either way.\",\n        \"confidence\": \"low\",\n        \"source\": \"c21\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"constraints\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k1\",\n        \"text\": \"Accuracy is primary and cost is the least priority; a cheaper path is valid only when it preserves accuracy.\",\n        \"type\": \"stakeholder\",\n        \"source\": \"c3\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k2\",\n        \"text\": \"The context builder's shaper has no token budget, no summarize-down and no truncation knobs, and includes everything relevant; this Epic holds every analyzer lookup and answer layout to the same rule.\",\n        \"type\": \"invariant\",\n        \"source\": \"c4\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k3\",\n        \"text\": \"No analyzer result may be reduced without the result saying so.\",\n        \"type\": \"stakeholder\",\n        \"source\": \"c5\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k4\",\n        \"text\": \"Calls that reach a model are made one after another, never in parallel.\",\n        \"type\": \"convention\",\n        \"source\": \"c3\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k5\",\n        \"text\": \"Schemas, catalogs and other structural reference go at the end of a prompt, not the middle.\",\n        \"type\": \"convention\",\n        \"source\": \"c3\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k6\",\n        \"text\": \"A simple text search remains a plain search; the analyzer is for questions that depend on relationships or meaning.\",\n        \"type\": \"stakeholder\",\n        \"source\": \"c7\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"k7\",\n        \"text\": \"Every claim in an analysis is grounded in a real exploration output, with no invented paths.\",\n        \"type\": \"invariant\",\n        \"source\": \"c9\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"stories\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s1\",\n        \"title\": \"Every result and every answer says whether it is complete\",\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"L\",\n        \"existingCapabilityRefs\": [\n          \"c1\"\n        ],\n        \"userValue\": \"As someone relying on an analysis, I am told plainly when a result was cut, when a lookup failed and when the analyzer could not produce an answer, so I never act on something that silently left things out.\",\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"any lookup or analysis step the analyzer performs, on either path a request can take through the analyzer\",\n            \"when\": \"its result is produced\",\n            \"then\": \"the result states whether it is complete, and if it is not, how many results were returned and why some are missing, and how many results exist when that can be established; when it cannot be (a source that cannot be read, a search that stopped before it finished, a source that can only be sampled), the result says that the total is unknown and why, and does not state a number\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"a lookup that cannot be carried out\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer reports on it\",\n            \"then\": \"it is reported as failed with the reason, and never as a lookup that found nothing\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac3\",\n            \"given\": \"a single item, such as a long document section, of which only part was read\",\n            \"when\": \"its result is produced\",\n            \"then\": \"the result names the item and says how much of it was read\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac4\",\n            \"given\": \"files that a text lookup did not read, because of their size, their kind or an error\",\n            \"when\": \"its result is produced\",\n            \"then\": \"the result says which were left out and why, or by what rule\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac5\",\n            \"given\": \"any answer, on either path a request can take through the analyzer\",\n            \"when\": \"it is delivered\",\n            \"then\": \"it states whether its findings are complete and names every result that was cut, partly read or failed\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac6\",\n            \"given\": \"the step that writes the answer fails\",\n            \"when\": \"the request ends\",\n            \"then\": \"the failure is reported with what the lookups found, and the request is not passed silently to another way of answering\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"functionalRequirements\": [\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"Each lookup or analysis-step result carries a statement of completeness.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"A failed lookup is distinguishable from an empty one.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"A partly read item and a file left out of a text lookup are reported.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"Every answer states whether its findings are complete.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"A failure to write the answer is reported, not hidden.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"dependsOn\": [\n          \"s6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s2\",\n        \"title\": \"The analyzer sizes a request from what it actually touches\",\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"dependsOn\": [\n          \"s1\",\n          \"s7\"\n        ],\n        \"existingCapabilityRefs\": [\n          \"c2\",\n          \"c11\"\n        ],\n        \"userValue\": \"As someone asking a question, the analyzer finds out how big my question really is before it answers, so a large question is recognised as large and is not treated like a small one.\",\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"a request, however it reaches the analyzer, including through the tools coding agents use\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer begins work on it\",\n            \"then\": \"it determines the size of the request from counts of what the request touches, and no size is taken from the wording alone or assumed\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"two requests with similar wording, one touching a small area and one touching a large area\",\n            \"when\": \"each is sized\",\n            \"then\": \"they are given different sizes that reflect what each touches\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac3\",\n            \"given\": \"a request that has been sized\",\n            \"when\": \"its answer is delivered\",\n            \"then\": \"the answer states the size that was determined and the counts it was determined from\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac4\",\n            \"given\": \"a request whose size cannot be determined\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer proceeds\",\n            \"then\": \"it says so and treats the request as the largest size, never as a small one\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\",\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac5\",\n            \"given\": \"a caller that states a size for its request\",\n            \"when\": \"the request is sized\",\n            \"then\": \"the stated size is kept as a hint and the measured size is used\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"functionalRequirements\": [\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"Request size is measured, not guessed from wording or assumed.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"The measured size and its basis are reported with the answer.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s3\",\n        \"title\": \"Each request size has a defined way of being handled, in full\",\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"L\",\n        \"dependsOn\": [\n          \"s1\",\n          \"s2\",\n          \"s7\"\n        ],\n        \"userValue\": \"As someone asking a large question, the analyzer works through all of it by a known method for its size and gives me one combined answer, so the size of my question never decides how much of it gets looked at.\",\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"each size a request can have, on either path a request can take through the analyzer\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer's handling of that size is examined\",\n            \"then\": \"there is a stated way of handling it that covers the whole of the request\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k2\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"a request whose results are too many to be reasoned over at once\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer handles it\",\n            \"then\": \"the results are divided into parts, every part is reasoned over, and the findings are combined into one answer with none lost\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k2\",\n              \"k4\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac3\",\n            \"given\": \"a request handled in parts\",\n            \"when\": \"its answer is delivered\",\n            \"then\": \"the answer states how many parts there were and that all were processed, or names any part that was not and why\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac4\",\n            \"given\": \"a small request whose complete input fits within what one model call accepts\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer handles it\",\n            \"then\": \"its results are returned whole without being divided; a small request whose input does not fit is handled in parts by the method for the case, with complete coverage and with the handling reported\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac5\",\n            \"given\": \"a part that fails while a large request is being handled\",\n            \"when\": \"the answer is assembled\",\n            \"then\": \"the findings of the other parts are kept and the failed part is reported as not covered\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac6\",\n            \"given\": \"a single item, such as a long document section, that is too large to be read at once\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer reads it\",\n            \"then\": \"its whole content is taken into account, not only its beginning\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k2\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac7\",\n            \"given\": \"a broad analysis of documents whose final combining step is handed more than one model call accepts, as on this repository on 2026-10-08, where Story s7 was accepted with that analysis not completing\",\n            \"when\": \"it is run\",\n            \"then\": \"the input to the combining step is handled in parts and the analysis returns a final report\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\",\n              \"k2\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"functionalRequirements\": [\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"A handling method exists for every request size on both paths.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"Large result sets are processed completely, in parts, and combined.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"A single item too large to read at once is read in full, in sections.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"The answer reports how the request was handled.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"A broad analysis whose final combining step is handed more than one model call accepts is completed by handling that input in parts; this closes the exception accepted on Story s7 for the docs family.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s4\",\n        \"title\": \"No lookup drops results\",\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"L\",\n        \"dependsOn\": [\n          \"s1\",\n          \"s3\",\n          \"s7\"\n        ],\n        \"existingCapabilityRefs\": [\n          \"c1\"\n        ],\n        \"userValue\": \"As someone relying on an analysis, I get every result a lookup found, whatever the size of my question, because nothing in the analyzer stops at a fixed number.\",\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"a lookup or analysis step whose true number of results is larger than any limit the analyzer used to apply, on either path a request can take through the analyzer, in a source that has something to count\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer performs it\",\n            \"then\": \"every result is returned and none is dropped\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k2\",\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"a single item larger than any fixed cut the analyzer used to apply to an item's content, or larger than the part of it the index stores\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer reads it\",\n            \"then\": \"no fixed cut is applied to it: the analyzer reads the item from its file at the place the index points to, after checking that the file still holds the item there; when the file has changed so that the item cannot be confirmed, or is missing or unreadable, the item is reported as not covered and the answer does not claim to have read it\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k2\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac3\",\n            \"given\": \"a text lookup over files of any size and lines of any length\",\n            \"when\": \"it runs\",\n            \"then\": \"no file is left out for its size, no matching line is shortened, and no part of the search's output is discarded\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k2\",\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac4\",\n            \"given\": \"the analyzer's own instructions and examples to the model that plans a lookup\",\n            \"when\": \"they are read\",\n            \"then\": \"none of them states or suggests a fixed number of results to ask for\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k2\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac5\",\n            \"given\": \"a result set that became larger because a limit was removed\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer answers\",\n            \"then\": \"it is handled by the method for its size and every result that can be obtained is processed; the answer says which sources were only sampled, failed or not covered, and it is called complete only where its evidence supports that\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\",\n              \"k2\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac6\",\n            \"given\": \"a data source with no tables or namespaces of its own, where the analyzer can only list what a sample of its keys suggests (Redis, etcd)\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer lists it\",\n            \"then\": \"the result says it is a sample and is not presented as complete; the analyzer does not scan every key of a live store\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"functionalRequirements\": [\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"No lookup or analysis step drops results because of a fixed limit, in any kind of source the analyzer covers that has something to count; a source that can only be sampled is reported as sampled.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"No fixed cut is applied to an item's content.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"A text lookup discards no file, line or output for its size.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"The planning instructions suggest no fixed number of results.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"Where an item's content matters to the answer, the analyzer reads the item from its file at the place the index points to; it does not rely on the body the index stores.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s5\",\n        \"title\": \"The form of an answer fits the question, for every kind of analyzer\",\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"L\",\n        \"dependsOn\": [\n          \"s1\",\n          \"s2\",\n          \"s3\",\n          \"s4\"\n        ],\n        \"existingCapabilityRefs\": [\n          \"c12\",\n          \"c13\"\n        ],\n        \"userValue\": \"As someone reading an analysis, the answer is laid out for the question I asked, including when I asked for every occurrence of something, and no layout holds back findings.\",\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"a question that asks for every occurrence of something\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer answers it\",\n            \"then\": \"the answer lists every occurrence the analysis established with where each is, says which sources were sampled, failed or not covered, claims complete coverage only where its evidence supports it, and is not forced into an overview of a module\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k2\",\n              \"k6\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"each answer layout the analyzer has, for code, documents, rule adherence, capability discovery, data and infrastructure, and the older per-source layouts it falls back to\",\n            \"when\": \"its answer layout is examined\",\n            \"then\": \"the layout places no limit on how many findings may be reported\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k2\",\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac3\",\n            \"given\": \"an answer layout\",\n            \"when\": \"it describes the lookup results it may draw on\",\n            \"then\": \"every kind of lookup that analyzer can run is described\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac4\",\n            \"given\": \"a question whose kind does not match the layout that would be used\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer answers\",\n            \"then\": \"it uses a layout for that kind of question and does not require parts of a layout the question has nothing to fill\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"localConstraints\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"lc1\",\n            \"text\": \"Structural reference in a prompt goes at its end.\",\n            \"type\": \"convention\",\n            \"source\": \"c3\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"functionalRequirements\": [\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"A question asking for every occurrence gets an enumeration of every occurrence the analysis established, with where each is; any source that was sampled, failed or not covered is stated, and the answer claims complete coverage only where its evidence supports it.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"The answer layouts of all analyzer kinds are free of limits on findings.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"Each layout covers every lookup its analyzer can run.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s6\",\n        \"title\": \"An unfocused request gets an answer, and a request that cannot proceed says why\",\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"existingCapabilityRefs\": [\n          \"c21\"\n        ],\n        \"userValue\": \"As someone asking the analyzer a broad question about a repository or a module, I get an analysis back, and when the analyzer cannot proceed I am told the actual reason, not that the model is unavailable when it was never asked.\",\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"a request that names an area but asks no specific question\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer builds the context for it\",\n            \"then\": \"it produces that context, where today it produces none and the request fails\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"a request started with a stated kind of source, which today is always treated as asking no specific question\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer handles it\",\n            \"then\": \"it proceeds as far as any other request does\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac3\",\n            \"given\": \"a request the analyzer cannot proceed with\",\n            \"when\": \"it fails\",\n            \"then\": \"the failure names the actual cause, and says the model is unavailable only when a call to the model failed\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\",\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac4\",\n            \"given\": \"a request that names a single file or a single symbol\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer builds the context for it\",\n            \"then\": \"it either produces that context or reports that such a request is not supported, and never reports the model as unavailable\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"functionalRequirements\": [\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"A request that asks no specific question gets its context built and can proceed.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"A failure to proceed reports its actual cause.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s7\",\n        \"title\": \"A broad analysis completes from request to final report\",\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"L\",\n        \"dependsOn\": [\n          \"s6\"\n        ],\n        \"existingCapabilityRefs\": [\n          \"c21\"\n        ],\n        \"userValue\": \"As someone asking the analyzer a broad question, the whole analysis runs to a final report, so the work this Epic does on completeness, sizing and handling has a working path to apply to.\",\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"a broad request on a repository that is indexed\",\n            \"when\": \"the analysis is run\",\n            \"then\": \"it completes every stage and returns a final report, and what stopped it at any stage it did not pass today is found and corrected\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"an analysis whose plan includes steps that themselves plan further steps\",\n            \"when\": \"it is run\",\n            \"then\": \"those nested steps run and their results reach the final report\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k7\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac3\",\n            \"given\": \"an analysis that stops part of the way through\",\n            \"when\": \"it ends\",\n            \"then\": \"the record of the run says at which stage it stopped and why, and is not left reading as still in progress\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k3\"\n            ]\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac4\",\n            \"given\": \"a completed analysis\",\n            \"when\": \"it is asked for again by the same run\",\n            \"then\": \"the stored result is returned as before\",\n            \"operationalizes\": [\n              \"k1\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"functionalRequirements\": [\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"A broad analysis runs through every stage to a final report.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"A run that stops records where and why.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"statement\": \"Accepted exception (stakeholder, 2026-10-08): for the docs family the first criterion is not met by this Story on a repository whose combining step is handed more than one model call accepts; Story s3 closes it. For the code family it is met in full only with Story s8.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s8\",\n        \"title\": \"The code tasks of a broad analysis work on a repository whose graph has no modules for its directories\",\n        \"userValue\": \"As someone asking for a broad analysis of a codebase, I get its modules and what each one offers, in any language the index covers, so the report is about my code and not a list of tasks that could not run.\",\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"a repository whose stored graph holds no entity of kind 'module' for its own directories, as for a TypeScript repository today\",\n            \"when\": \"a broad code analysis lists the repository's modules and its module tree\",\n            \"then\": \"the directories that hold source are returned as its modules, and the result says what it rests on\",\n            \"operationalizes\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"a plan in which the planner names a directory of the repository as the module to describe\",\n            \"when\": \"the task that describes a module's functional surface runs\",\n            \"then\": \"it returns what that directory offers, and does not fail for want of a stored module entity\",\n            \"operationalizes\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac3\",\n            \"given\": \"a repository whose graph does hold entities of kind 'module' for its own directories (no parser stores them today: each stores a module only for an imported module; a graph written by other means may hold them)\",\n            \"when\": \"the same tasks run\",\n            \"then\": \"they return at least what they return today\",\n            \"operationalizes\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac4\",\n            \"given\": \"a module value that names nothing in the repository\",\n            \"when\": \"a task is given it\",\n            \"then\": \"the task fails with a reason that says so, and is not reported as an empty module\",\n            \"operationalizes\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac5\",\n            \"given\": \"a broad code analysis of an indexed repository, once this Story and Story s7 are built\",\n            \"when\": \"it is run\",\n            \"then\": \"it returns a final report in which the functional-surface tasks succeeded\",\n            \"operationalizes\": []\n          }\n        ],\n        \"sizeEstimate\": \"M\",\n        \"dependsOn\": [\n          \"s7\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"s9\",\n        \"title\": \"A request's size decides how deep and detailed its plan is, and a plan is checked to be executable\",\n        \"userValue\": \"Someone asking a broad question about a large codebase gets a plan that is wide and shallow and that the analyzer can finish, while someone asking about a small area gets a plan that goes deep, so a broad analysis reaches its final report in a reasonable time instead of spending the run inside deeper and deeper child plans.\",\n        \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac1\",\n            \"given\": \"A request that measures XL or L\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer plans it\",\n            \"then\": \"the plan is breadth-first: many shallow, inexpensive tasks across the areas; a child plan is allowed where the policy for the size of the whole request provides one, but a child plan of an XL or L request does not plan further children, so no area is explored by a chain of deeper plans\",\n            \"operationalizes\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac2\",\n            \"given\": \"A request that measures M or S\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer plans it\",\n            \"then\": \"the plan is depth-first: fewer areas, each examined in detail, and child plans are allowed where they add depth\",\n            \"operationalizes\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac3\",\n            \"given\": \"a plan whose total number of tasks, counted over the root plan and every child plan below it, would exceed the limit the size of the request sets (every size has one; for XS the existing policy is kept)\",\n            \"when\": \"the plan is validated\",\n            \"then\": \"it is refused with a reason that names what was counted, the total and the limit, so that the planner can correct it, in the same way a wrong task count is refused today\",\n            \"operationalizes\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac4\",\n            \"given\": \"a plan accepted for a broad request\",\n            \"when\": \"the analyzer executes it and the budget set by the request's size is reached\",\n            \"then\": \"the run ends as explicitly incomplete: the findings produced so far are kept in the report, the work not done is listed as not covered, and the run is not reported as a complete analysis; a run that stays within its budget is not affected\",\n            \"operationalizes\": []\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"ac5\",\n            \"given\": \"the broad docs request on this repository, which measured XL, run on a stated revision\",\n            \"when\": \"it is run end to end with the time limit that the size policy sets for an XL request, fixed and recorded before the run starts\",\n            \"then\": \"it reaches a final report within that limit, measured from the request received to the final report, and its record says how deep the plan went and how many tasks ran\",\n            \"operationalizes\": []\n          }\n        ],\n        \"dependsOn\": [\n          \"s2\",\n          \"s3\",\n          \"s7\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"openQuestions\": [\n      \"Story s7 rests on a low-confidence assumption: no completed broad analysis is on record. Its design begins by running one and recording how far it gets; if what is found is larger than one Story, how should it be split?\"\n    ],\n    \"functionalDefinition\": {\n      \"requirements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:FR001\",\n          \"statement\": \"Every analyzer result states whether it is complete, a lookup that failed is reported as failed and never as empty, and every answer states whether its findings are complete.\",\n          \"scope\": \"doc\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:FR002\",\n          \"statement\": \"The analyzer determines the size of a request from what the request actually touches, on both paths a request can take.\",\n          \"scope\": \"doc\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:FR003\",\n          \"statement\": \"For each size of request the analyzer follows a defined way of handling it, and a result set or a single item too large to treat at once is processed in full, in parts, and combined.\",\n          \"scope\": \"doc\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:FR004\",\n          \"statement\": \"No lookup or analysis step drops results because of a fixed limit, and no limit is removed before the analyzer can handle what it lets through.\",\n          \"scope\": \"doc\",\n          \"rationale\": \"A fixed limit makes large questions silently wrong; removing one without handling makes them fail.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:FR005\",\n          \"statement\": \"The form of an analyzer's answer fits the kind of question asked, including a question that asks for every occurrence of something, for each kind of source the analyzer covers.\",\n          \"scope\": \"doc\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:FR006\",\n          \"statement\": \"No answer layout limits how many findings may be reported.\",\n          \"scope\": \"doc\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:FR007\",\n          \"statement\": \"A request that asks no specific question is analysed from request to final report, and a request that cannot proceed says why.\",\n          \"scope\": \"doc\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S001:FR001\",\n          \"statement\": \"Each lookup or analysis-step result carries a statement of completeness.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S001:FR002\",\n          \"statement\": \"A failed lookup is distinguishable from an empty one.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S001:FR003\",\n          \"statement\": \"A partly read item and a file left out of a text lookup are reported.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S001:FR004\",\n          \"statement\": \"Every answer states whether its findings are complete.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S001:FR005\",\n          \"statement\": \"A failure to write the answer is reported, not hidden.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S002:FR001\",\n          \"statement\": \"Request size is measured, not guessed from wording or assumed.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S002:FR002\",\n          \"statement\": \"The measured size and its basis are reported with the answer.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s2\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S003:FR001\",\n          \"statement\": \"A handling method exists for every request size on both paths.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S003:FR002\",\n          \"statement\": \"Large result sets are processed completely, in parts, and combined.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S003:FR003\",\n          \"statement\": \"A single item too large to read at once is read in full, in sections.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S003:FR004\",\n          \"statement\": \"The answer reports how the request was handled.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S003:FR005\",\n          \"statement\": \"A broad analysis whose final combining step is handed more than one model call accepts is completed by handling that input in parts; this closes the exception accepted on Story s7 for the docs family.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s3\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S004:FR001\",\n          \"statement\": \"No lookup or analysis step drops results because of a fixed limit, in any kind of source the analyzer covers that has something to count; a source that can only be sampled is reported as sampled.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s4\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S004:FR002\",\n          \"statement\": \"No fixed cut is applied to an item's content.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s4\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S004:FR003\",\n          \"statement\": \"A text lookup discards no file, line or output for its size.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s4\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S004:FR004\",\n          \"statement\": \"The planning instructions suggest no fixed number of results.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s4\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S004:FR005\",\n          \"statement\": \"Where an item's content matters to the answer, the analyzer reads the item from its file at the place the index points to; it does not rely on the body the index stores.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s4\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S005:FR001\",\n          \"statement\": \"A question asking for every occurrence gets an enumeration of every occurrence the analysis established, with where each is; any source that was sampled, failed or not covered is stated, and the answer claims complete coverage only where its evidence supports it.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s5\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S005:FR002\",\n          \"statement\": \"The answer layouts of all analyzer kinds are free of limits on findings.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s5\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S005:FR003\",\n          \"statement\": \"Each layout covers every lookup its analyzer can run.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s5\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S006:FR001\",\n          \"statement\": \"A request that asks no specific question gets its context built and can proceed.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s6\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S006:FR002\",\n          \"statement\": \"A failure to proceed reports its actual cause.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s6\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S007:FR001\",\n          \"statement\": \"A broad analysis runs through every stage to a final report.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s7\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S007:FR002\",\n          \"statement\": \"A run that stops records where and why.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s7\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E20261006b9d5c5c4:S007:FR003\",\n          \"statement\": \"Accepted exception (stakeholder, 2026-10-08): for the docs family the first criterion is not met by this Story on a repository whose combining step is handed more than one model call accepts; Story s3 closes it. For the code family it is met in full only with Story s8.\",\n          \"scope\": \"item\",\n          \"itemRef\": \"s7\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"kind\": \"analyze-bundle\",\n      \"ref\": \"Lookups in src/analyze that return at most a fixed number of results (file:line of the constant, default / maximum): explore/search-text.ts:39-40 (30 / 200); explore/symbol-locate.ts:37-38 (50 / 200); explore/config-trace.ts:42-43 (40 / 200); explore/test-locate.ts:44-45 (20 / 100); explore/import-graph.ts:48-49 (15 / 60); explore/usage-example.ts:37-38 (12 / 40); explore/doc-mention.ts:37-38 (15 / 40); explore/concept-resolve.ts:64 (20); explore/capability-reuse-check.ts:58-59 (5 / 12); explore/db-tables-list.ts:36-37 (40 / 500); explore/manifests-locate.ts:51-52 (200 / 1,000); explore/data-model-trace.ts:47-49 (4 targets, 12 fields, 6 callers); explore/convention-detect.ts:54, :57 (5 subclasses, 8 idioms); runtimes/data/discovery-objects.ts:56 (200 files); runtimes/infra/_shared.ts:90 (5,000 files); runtimes/infra/discovery-families.ts:53 (8 samples). Cuts on the content of one item: explore/doc-constraint-enumerate.ts:227 and explore/doc-decision-trace.ts:242 (first 2,000 characters); runtimes/code/adherence-check.ts:92, runtimes/data/adherence-check.ts:100 and runtimes/infra/adherence-check.ts:89 (first 1,200); explore/module-profile.ts:222, :284 (first 4,096); summariser/driver.ts:317 (first 8,192). Not counted: text-length limits on plan fields (planner/schema.ts:42-44), which bound a model's own wording, not results. Found by an analyzer run of 2026-10-06 (two search.text explorations and a module.profile over src/analyze) and confirmed by reading each file. Found by the HLD's review and added: the maxSources parameter of the two document lookups (explore/executor.ts:315, :337); src/analyze/docs-retrieval.ts:290; explore/capability-reuse-check.ts:303, :348-350; explore/db-table-describe.ts:175, :181; runtimes/docs/family-summarise.ts:162; the preview limits explore/doc-mention.ts:39-40; and, in the shared grep primitive src/daemon/tools/builtins/search/grep.ts, the cut of a matching line at 500 characters (:107), the skip of files over 2 MB (:102), the silent skip of unreadable files (:111) and the per-file match limit (:178)