","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/8","selector":"/citations/8","title":"Citation 9","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/9","selector":"/citations/9","title":"Citation 10","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/10","selector":"/citations/10","title":"Citation 11","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/11","selector":"/citations/11","title":"Citation 12","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/12","selector":"/citations/12","title":"Citation 13","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/13","selector":"/citations/13","title":"Citation 14","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/14","selector":"/citations/14","title":"Citation 15","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/15","selector":"/citations/15","title":"Citation 16","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/16","selector":"/citations/16","title":"Citation 17","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/17","selector":"/citations/17","title":"Citation 18","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/18","selector":"/citations/18","title":"Citation 19","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/19","selector":"/citations/19","title":"Citation 20","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/20","selector":"/citations/20","title":"Citation 21","kind":"citation"},{"id":"document:line:26","selector":"document:line:26","title":"2. Functional requirements","kind":"section"},{"id":"document:line:301","selector":"document:line:301","title":"Resolved questions","kind":"section"}]},"completedChunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the live DEF, canonical artifact, recorded requirements, cited repository evidence and upstream designs. Rollout prerequisites are now coherent, but citation identity and budget-versus-completeness requirements still need reconciliation. No authored or generated visual is attached or necessary for this epic-level definition.","findings":[{"id":"scope2-citation-01","severity":"MED","location":"/citations/20/id","message":"Renaming the sampling decision to c22 creates another collision: citations/19 already uses c22 for the triage record. The two distinct evidence records therefore cannot be addressed uniquely in either the canonical artifact or Markdown. Assign the sampling decision an unused identity while preserving the existing triage citation.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/19",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/20","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:294","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:295","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:327","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:328"]},{"id":"scope2-budget-contract-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2","message":"The new budget-exhaustion outcome is explicit, but its exception has not been reconciled with the complete-processing requirements. FR003 requires oversized inputs to be processed in full; s3/ac2 requires every part to be reasoned over; and s4/ac5 requires every obtainable result to be processed. A healthy run that reaches s9/ac4's budget must instead stop with work unprocessed. Define which completeness obligations apply to successful runs and explicitly qualify them for budget-stopped runs across the functional definition and story criteria, so acceptance does not simultaneously require both outcomes.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/4",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:31","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:162","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:187","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:270"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/flavor","/body/problem","/body/nonGoals","/body/assumptions","/body/constraints","/body/stories","/body/openQuestions","/body/functionalDefinition","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/3","/body/constraints/4","/body/constraints/5","/body/constraints/6","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/citations/9","/citations/10","/citations/11","/citations/12","/citations/13","/citations/14","/citations/15","/citations/16","/citations/17","/citations/18","/citations/19","/citations/20","document:line:26","document:line:301","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-framework.md — scope/depth policy, citations, recursive execution and accuracy convention","design/analyze-context-builder.md — lossless relevance window, ownership, caching and failure contracts","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — incremental child plans, per-plan validation, depth ceilings, persistence and partial failures","CLAUDE.md — accuracy, provider access and trailing structural reference","site/analyze.html:61 — exploration-grounded claims",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-12f70133491114c9.json — excluded graph-edge defects","src/analyze/measure.ts — measured sizing, unknown counts and caller hints","src/analyze/planner/scope-band.ts — existing per-plan task bands","src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1590 — broad-request pipeline and measured scope","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:727 — source-hinted intent handling","sr