sertions","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/__tests__/source-modules.test.ts — identity, ownership and refusal scenario inventory","src/indexer/parser/typescript.ts — module-entity occurrence inspection","src/indexer/parser/python.ts — imported modules have empty repository/file","src/indexer/parser/go.ts — imported modules have empty repository/file","src/indexer/parser/java.ts — imported modules have empty repository/file","src/indexer/parser/scala.ts — imported modules have empty repository/file"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Use explicit acceptance fixtures for mixed-language directories, descendant-only source, overlapping stored modules, and relative versus absolute module values; the shared runtime supplies concrete rules for these cases.","Tests and live analyses were not executed. This read-only DEF assessment inspected source contracts and assertions."]},{"chunkId":"reporting","status":"passed","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed. The revised reporting requirements distinguish exact and unknown totals, preserve returned counts and reasons, separate failures from empty results, and require disclosures for partial reads and omitted files on both analyzer paths. Surrounding criteria cover sampled sources, stale-pointer refusals, failed partitions and budget-stopped work while retaining established findings. Answer-write failures must preserve lookup evidence without silent fallback, and completeness remains qualified by the evidence source. No blocking design defect was demonstrated within this assignment. No visual artifact is attached or necessary for these epic-level reporting contracts.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/5","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/0","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/7","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/8","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/9","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/10","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/11","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/6","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","DEF.md:126-131 — completeness, counts, failure distinction, partial reads, omissions and answer-write failure","DEF.md:90 — graph repair excluded; completeness limited to what this Epic establishes","DEF.md:161-167 — partition reporting, retained findings and failed-part coverage","DEF.md:181-188 — authoritative-content validation, uncovered items and live-store sampling","DEF.md:203-206 — evidence-qualified answer coverage","DEF.md:270 — budget exhaustion retains findings and lists work not executed","design/analyze-context-builder.md — lossless context and distinct failure contracts","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — upstream materialization, missing dependencies and partial completeness","design/analyze-framework.md — task failure propagation and evidence grounding","src/analyze/completeness.ts — result counts, unknown totals, partial reads, derived answer reports and handling disclosures","src/analyze/explore/answer-report.ts — lookup-to-answer propagation and missing-record handling","src/analyze/explore/completeness-facts.ts — graph-relative completeness, text omissions and carried metadata","src/analyze/context/schema.ts — stored report schema and exclusion of model-authored completeness","src/analyze/context/driver.ts — retained lookup evidence and classified answer-write failures","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts — context/task report composition and answer-failure mapping","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/aggregator.ts — absent inputs, partition handling and retained upstream evidence","src/daemon/steps/analyze-step/phases/bundle.ts — server-derived completeness and terminal schema-failure evidence","src/daemon/steps/analyze-step/answer-turn.ts — missing-prompt and answer-step failure contracts","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.code.system.md — failed lookups and model-directed coverage disclosures","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.data.system.md — failed versus empty data-source results","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.adherence.system.md — omitted and partly read search evidence","src/analyze/explore/__tests__/completeness-all-lookups.test.ts:375 — exact/unknown totals, source limits, returned counts and partial-read assertions","src/daemon/steps/__tests__/analyze-step-bundle-report.test.ts — delivered report propagation and rejection of forged completeness","src/analyze/context/__tests__/answer-failure-mapping.test.ts — evidence, uncovered parts and cause chains preserved through both failure mappings","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/nested-aggregate-failure.test.ts:52 — nested failures and handling disclosures reach the final report","src/analyze/runtimes/__tests__/completeness-all-runtimes.test.ts — runtime completeness and sampling test inventory"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Extend regression assertions for the revised unknown-total rule to unreadable and skipped sources without a reached limit: buildCompleteness currently defaults total to returned in that case unless the caller explicitly supplies null.","Tests were inspected as evidence; executing tests or live-store analyses was unnecessary for this read-only DEF assessment."]},{"chunkId":"sizing","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were inspected against the live DEF, canonical artifact, upstream designs, and relevant planner, executor and test contracts. Measured sizing, caller hints, unknown-size fallback and sampling exceptions are coherent. The revised s9 prerequisites are feasible. Two acceptance inconsistencies remain around budget-stopped coverage and the timed completion benchmark. No visual artifact is attached or necessary for this epic-level capability definition.","findings":[{"id":"sizing2-budget-coverage-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","message":"Explicitly reporting budget exhaustion fixes silent termination, but the resulting coverage exception still contradicts the complete-handling requirements. A healthy run must stop with obtainable work unprocessed under s9/ac4, while FR003, s3/ac2 and s4/ac5 require full processing. k1 and the non-goal excluding time/model-cost reduction further constrain this tradeoff. Reconcile these requirements by explicitly distinguishing successful complete processing from budget-stopped incomplete termination, and state whether uncovered work can subsequently be completed.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:31 — FR003 requires processing oversized results in full","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:162 — s3/ac2 requires every part to be processed","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:187 — s4/ac5 requires every obtainable result to be processed","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:270 — s9/ac4 requires termination with uncovered work","design/analyze-context-builder.md:167 — accuracy-first, lossless inclusion contract"]},{"id":"sizing2-timed-completion-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","message":"The revised criterion makes the revision, predetermined XL limit and measurement interval observable, but only requires a final report within that limit. Because ac4 now expressly produces a final report on budget exhaustion, this benchmark can pass after doing little work and returning an incomplete report. That does not demonstrate the docs end-to-end completion promised by s3/ac7 and s9's user value. Require this benchmark to finish the intended analysis without budget-induced uncovered work, while testing incomplete budget termination separately.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:167 — s3/ac7 closes the broad docs completion exception","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts:40 — existing broad docs regression","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts:62 — existing assertions require a report but only check that completeness is boolean"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/8","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/1","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/12","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/13","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:11 — incremental child-plan model","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:83 — independently measured per-plan task bands","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:138 — corrective retry contract","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:155 — XL partition children","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:194 — root scope depth ceilings","design/ana