g those runs is optional for this scope assessment."]},{"chunkId":"broad","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were inspected against the live DEF, canonical artifact, upstream designs, and relevant runtime and test sources. The s6–s8 capability boundaries and module-discovery approach are feasible, but s7's unconditional completion promises conflict with s9's budget-stopped outcome. No visual artifact is attached to this DEF; prose is sufficient for this epic-level scope.","findings":[{"id":"broad2-terminal-contract-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/0","message":"Reconcile s7's lifecycle acceptance with s9's new budget-exhaustion outcome. s7/ac1 requires every stage to complete, s7/ac2 requires nested steps to run and reach the final report, and S007:FR001 repeats the unconditional completion promise. An accepted plan stopped by s9/ac4 deliberately leaves work unexecuted, even when no task fails. S007:FR003 qualifies completion only for the docs aggregation and code-module prerequisites; neither covers this new outcome. Distinguish full completion from an explicitly incomplete terminal report, qualify the nested-execution promise accordingly, and specify whether retrieving that terminal report under the same run follows s7/ac4's stored-result behavior.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/0",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/1",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/3",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/29",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/31","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:235","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:270","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts — stored-result repla