and refusal scenario inventory","src/indexer/parser/typescript.ts — module-entity occurrence inspection","src/indexer/parser/python.ts — imported modules have empty repository/file","src/indexer/parser/go.ts — imported modules have empty repository/file","src/indexer/parser/java.ts — imported modules have empty repository/file","src/indexer/parser/scala.ts — imported modules have empty repository/file"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Use explicit acceptance fixtures for mixed-language directories, descendant-only source, overlapping stored modules, and relative versus absolute module values; the shared runtime supplies concrete rules for these cases.","Tests and live analyses were not executed. This read-only DEF assessment inspected source contracts and assertions."]},{"chunkId":"reporting","status":"passed","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed. The revised reporting requirements distinguish exact and unknown totals, preserve returned counts and reasons, separate failures from empty results, and require disclosures for partial reads and omitted files on both analyzer paths. Surrounding criteria cover sampled sources, stale-pointer refusals, failed partitions and budget-stopped work while retaining established findings. Answer-write failures must preserve lookup evidence without silent fallback, and completeness remains qualified by the evidence source. No blocking design defect was demonstrated within this assignment. No visual artifact is attached or necessary for these epic-level reporting contracts.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/5","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/0","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/7","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/8","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/