er-turn.ts — missing-prompt and answer-step failure contracts","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.code.system.md — failed lookups and model-directed coverage disclosures","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.data.system.md — failed versus empty data-source results","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.adherence.system.md — omitted and partly read search evidence","src/analyze/explore/__tests__/completeness-all-lookups.test.ts:375 — exact/unknown totals, source limits, returned counts and partial-read assertions","src/daemon/steps/__tests__/analyze-step-bundle-report.test.ts — delivered report propagation and rejection of forged completeness","src/analyze/context/__tests__/answer-failure-mapping.test.ts — evidence, uncovered parts and cause chains preserved through both failure mappings","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/nested-aggregate-failure.test.ts:52 — nested failures and handling disclosures reach the final report","src/analyze/runtimes/__tests__/completeness-all-runtimes.test.ts — runtime completeness and sampling test inventory"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Extend regression assertions for the revised unknown-total rule to unreadable and skipped sources without a reached limit: buildCompleteness currently defaults total to returned in that case unless the caller explicitly supplies null.","Tests were inspected as evidence; executing tests or live-store analyses was unnecessary for this read-only DEF assessment."]},{"chunkId":"sizing","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were inspected against the live DEF, canonical artifact, upstream designs, and relevant planner, executor and test contracts. Measured sizing, caller hints, unknown-size fallback and sampling exceptions are coherent. The revised s9 prerequisites are feasible. Two acceptance inconsistencies remain around budget-stopped coverage and the timed completion benchmark. No visual artifact is attached or necessary for this epic-level capability definition.","findings":[{"id":"sizing2-budget-coverage-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","message":"Explicitly reporting budget exhaustion fixes silent termination, but the resulting coverage exception still contradicts the complete-handling requirements. A healthy run must stop with obtainable work unprocessed under s9/ac4, while FR003, s3/ac2 and s4/ac5 require full processing. k1 and the non-goal excluding time/model-cost reduction further constrain this tradeoff. Reconcile these requirements by explicitly distinguishing successful complete processing from budget-stopped incomplete termination, and state whether uncovered work can subsequently be completed.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:31 — FR003 requires processing oversized results in full","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:162 — s3/ac2 requires every part to be processed","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:187 — s4/ac5 requires every obtainable result to be processed","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:270 — s9/ac4 requires termination with uncovered work","design/analyze-context-builder.md:167 — accuracy-first, lossless inclusion contract"]},{"id":"sizing2-timed-completion-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","message":"The revised criterion makes the revision, predetermined XL limit and measurement interval observable, but only requires a final report within that limit. Because ac4 now expressly produces a final report on budget exhaustion, this benchmark can pass after doing little work and returning an incomplete report. That does not demonstrate the docs end-to-end completion promised by s3/ac7 and s9's user value. Require this benchmark to finish the intended analysis without budget-induced uncovered work, while testing incomplete budget termination separately.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:167 — s3/ac7 closes the broad docs completion exception","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts:40 — existing broad docs regression","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts:62 — existing assertions require a report but only check that completeness is boolean"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/8","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/1","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/12","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/13","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:11 — incremental child-plan model","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:83 — independently measured per-plan task bands","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:138 — corrective retry contract","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:155 — XL partition children","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:194 — root scope depth ceilings","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:246 — resumability and persisted child plans","design/analyze-framework.m