sted","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed. The revised small-request criterion correctly distinguishes measured size from model-call capacity. Whole-item processing, retained findings and citations, sequential calls, and failed-part reporting are coherent at DEF level. Complete-processing obligations still conflict with s9's budget termination. No additional diagram or UX artifact is necessary for this capability at this stage.","findings":[{"id":"handling2-budget-completeness-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1","message":"s3 requires every partition to be processed and combined without losing findings, while FR003 and S003:FR002 repeat unconditional complete processing. Under s9/ac4, an otherwise healthy run must stop when its budget is reached and leave work uncovered. Reporting that outcome honestly satisfies disclosure but does not satisfy these processing requirements. Explicitly distinguish complete execution from budget-stopped incomplete execution across s3 and its flattened requirements. Also clarify that an incomplete terminal report does not, by itself, demonstrate closure of the docs aggregation exception in ac7 and S003:FR005.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/15",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/18",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:162","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:167","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:270","design/analyze-context-builder.md:167 — accuracy-first, lossless inclusion contract"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/2","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stori