asurement, complete handling and retrieval before layout uncapping.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/4/dependsOn","DEF.md section 6.5","Checkpoint attempt 2: scope and answers assessments"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["scope","answers","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope-budget-02"},"rationale":"Current s9 permits children while prohibiting grandchildren for XL/L roots and specifies an explicitly incomplete budget terminal outcome. The residual contradiction with unconditional full-processing requirements is captured by the current replacement finding.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/0",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","Checkpoint attempt 2: scope finding scope2-budget-contract-02","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:155–194"],"action":"superseded","reviewedInChunkIds":["scope","sizing","handling","consistency"],"supersededBy":{"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope2-budget-contract-02"}},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope-citation-03"},"rationale":"The historical failure retains c21, but assigning c22 to sampling collides with the existing triage identity. The current replacement records this remaining citation defect.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/18",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/19",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/20","Checkpoint attempt 2: scope finding scope2-citation-01"],"action":"superseded","reviewedInChunkIds":["scope","consistency"],"supersededBy":{"chunkId":"scope","findingId":"scope2-citation-01"}},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"reporting","findingId":"reporting-unknown-total-01"},"rationale":"Revised s1/ac1 requires established totals when available and explicitly unknown totals with reasons for unreadable, stopped-search and sampled sources, while retaining returned counts.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/0","src/analyze/completeness.ts:61–70","Checkpoint attempt 2: reporting assessment"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["reporting","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"sizing","findingId":"sizing-prerequisites-01"},"rationale":"Current s9 explicitly depends on s2, s3 and s7, covering measurement, oversized aggregation handling and broad-analysis execution.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/dependsOn","DEF.md section 6.9","Checkpoint attempt 2: sizing assessment"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["sizing","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"sizing","findingId":"sizing-budget-completeness-02"},"rationale":"The revised criterion defines retained findings, uncovered work and an incomplete terminal report, and the child restriction is now root-based. The unresolved coverage exception is more precisely captured by the current replacement.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/0",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","Checkpoint attempt 2: sizing finding sizing2-budget-coverage-01"],"action":"superseded","reviewedInChunkIds":["sizing","handling","consistency"],"supersededBy":{"chunkId":"sizing","findingId":"sizing2-budget-coverage-01"}},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"sizing","findingId":"sizing-aggregate-policy-03"},"rationale":"Revised s9/ac3 explicitly counts tasks across the root and every descendant, requires a size-based limit for every size, retains the XS policy and requires count/total/limit rejection evidence.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/2","Checkpoint attempt 2: sizing assessment"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["sizing","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"sizing","findingId":"sizing-timing-acceptance-04"},"rationale":"Current ac5 identifies the broad docs fixture on a stated revision, fixes and records the XL policy limit before execution, and measures request receipt through final report. The separate incomplete-report loophole remains recorded as sizing2-timed-completion-02.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","Checkpoint attempt 2: sizing assessment and sizing2-timed-completion-02"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["sizing","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"handling","findingId":"handling-small-fit-01"},"rationale":"Revised s3/ac4 conditions undivided handling on complete input fitting one model call and permits complete, reported partitioning otherwise.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/3","src/analyze/context/handling.ts:105–145","Checkpoint attempt 2: handling assessment"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["handling","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"retrieval","findingId":"retrieval-stale-pointer-01"},"rationale":"Current s4/ac2 requires confirmation that the file still holds the indexed item and reports unconfirmed, missing or unreadable content as uncovered without claiming it was read.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/1","src/analyze/item-length.ts:43–94","Checkpoint attempt 2: retrieval assessment"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["retrieval","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"retrieval","findingId":"retrieval-sampling-completeness-02"},"rationale":"Revised s4/ac5 preserves sampled, failed and uncovered-source disclosures and qualifies complete-coverage claims by evidence. Flattened S004:FR001 now explicitly retains sampled-source reporting. The separate budget-processing contradiction remains recorded by current findings.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/4",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/19","Checkpoint attempt 2: retrieval assessment"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["retrieval","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"answers","findingId":"answers-prerequisites-01"},"rationale":"Current s5 declares all s1–s4 prerequisites, preserving the required progression before exhaustive presentation and removal of layout limits.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/4/dependsOn","Checkpoint attempt 2: answers assessment"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["answers","scope","consistency"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"answers","findingId":"answers-completeness-02"},"rationale":"Current s5/ac1, its local functional requirement and flattened S005:FR001 enumerate established occurrences with locations, disclose sampled/failed/uncovered sources and permit complete-coverage claims only when supported.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/4/acceptanceCriteria/0",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/4/functionalRequirements/0",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/24","Checkpoint attempt 2: answers assessment"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["answers","consistency"]}]}],"limitations":[],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"91358dd682d748eaa8995437fe233cce3cd5805438af01638b10fa0f01840c05","impact":{"baselineAttempt":1,"mode":"full","coverageOrigins":[{"chunkId":"scope","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"broad","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"reporting","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"sizing","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"handling","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"retrieval","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"answers","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"consistency","kind":"f