d":"section"}]},"completedChunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector, the live DEF, canonical artifact, applicable upstream designs and linked repository evidence. Rollout dependencies are coherent, but completeness obligations conflict with budget termination, and citation identities remain duplicated. No visual artifact is attached or necessary for this epic-level scope definition.","findings":[{"id":"scope3-budget-contract-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2","message":"The complete-processing requirements remain incompatible with the budget-exhaustion outcome. FR003 requires oversized inputs to be processed in full, s3/ac2 requires every part to be reasoned over, and s4/ac5 requires every obtainable result to be processed. However, s9/ac4 requires an otherwise healthy run to stop with work unprocessed when its budget is reached. Reporting that interruption honestly satisfies disclosure but does not satisfy those unconditional processing requirements. Explicitly reconcile budget-stopped runs with the functional requirements, story criteria and accuracy-first constraint so acceptance has one consistent contract.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/4",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:31","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:162","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:187","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:270","design/analyze-context-builder.md — Sizing","CLAUDE.md — Project principles"]},{"id":"scope3-citation-02","severity":"MED","location":"/citations/20/id","message":"Two distinct evidence records still share citation id c22: citations/19 identifies the triage decision adding s6/s7, while citations/20 identifies the Redis/etcd sampling decision. Both are rendered as [[c22]] in the document, preventing unique evidence references. Assign the sampling decision an unused identity and preserve the triage record's identity.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/19",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/20","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:294","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:295","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:327","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:328"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/flavor","/body/problem","/body/nonGoals","/body/assumptions","/body/constraints","/body/stories","/body/openQuestions","/body/functionalDefinition","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/3","/body/constraints/4","/body/constraints/5","/body/constraints/6","document:line:26","document:line:301","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/8","/citations/13","/citations/14","/citations/16","/citations/17","/citations/19","/citations/20","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-12f70133491114c9.json — separately tracked graph-edge defect","design/analyze-context-builder.md — relevance window, lossless sizing, ownership and failure contracts","design/analyze-framework.md:1 — purpose, non-goals, measured scope and depth policy","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — incremental child plans, validation, aggregation and failure propagation","CLAUDE.md — accuracy, serial model calls, daemon ownership, provider abstraction and prompt conventions","site/analyze.html — public analyzer contract and exploration-grounded claims","src/analyze/explore/search-text.ts:42 — retained lookup limits","src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1506 — pipeline failure causes","src/analyze/measure.ts — current measured sizing contract","src/analyze/planner/scope-band.ts — current per-plan task bands","src/prompts/steering-block.md:50 — search-versus-analysis guidance","git commit 83a1cc0bd19134d491748daff0614e5007d9c81f — separately applied steering change"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Add stable functional-requirement identities for s8 and s9; the functional definition currently stops at s7 despite both later stories having substantive acceptance criteria.","Update the resolved hook question's explanation: it still assigns steering changes to s5, while current s5 concerns answer layouts and steering changes are explicitly excluded from this Epic.","Label the problem statement and historical code references as the original baseline. Current measurement and broad-request handling already implement portions of the proposed corrections; the cited MCP start file no longer exists at its recorded path.","Carry the replacement root-depth policy into applicable upstream documentation when implemented. Historical external session logs were assessed as recorded observations; replaying those measurements is optional for this scope review."]},{"chunkId":"broad","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the live DEF, canonical artifact, upstream designs and relevant runtime/test sources. The s6–s8 dependency order is feasible, and the docs and code-module exceptions have explicit closure owners. One lifecycle acceptance conflict requires correction. No visual artifact is attached or necessary for this epic-level capability definition.","findings":[{"id":"broad3-terminal-contract-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/0","message":"Reconcile s7's completion contract with s9's budget-stopped outcome. s7/ac1 requires every stage to complete, s7/ac2 requires nested steps to run and reach the report, and S007:FR001 repeats unconditional completion. However, s9/ac4 requires an accepted broad run to stop with work unexecuted when its budget is reached. S007:FR003 qualifies completion only for docs aggregation and code-module prerequisites. Define the distinction between full completion and an incomplete terminal report, qualify nested-execution acceptance accordingly, and specify whether retrieving a budget-stopped report under the same run follows s7/ac4's stored-result behavior.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/0",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/1",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/3",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/29",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/31","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:235","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:270","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts — stored-result replay requires status=ok, stage=done, intent and finalReport","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts:343 — child execution materializes the child's terminal report"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/5","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/5/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/6","/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/