citations/19 already uses c22 for the triage record. The two distinct evidence records therefore cannot be addressed uniquely in either the canonical artifact or Markdown. Assign the sampling decision an unused identity while preserving the existing triage citation.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/19",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/20","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:294","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:295","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:327","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:328"]},{"id":"scope2-budget-contract-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2","message":"The new budget-exhaustion outcome is explicit, but its exception has not been reconciled with the complete-processing requirements. FR003 requires oversized inputs to be processed in full; s3/ac2 requires every part to be reasoned over; and s4/ac5 requires every obtainable result to be processed. A healthy run that reaches s9/ac4's budget must instead stop with work unprocessed. Define which completeness obligations apply to successful runs and explicitly qualify them for budget-stopped runs across the functional definition and story criteria, so acceptance does not simultaneously require both outcomes.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/4",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:31","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:162","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:187","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:270"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/flavor","/body/problem","/body/nonGoals","/body/assumptions","/body/constraints","/body/stories","/body/openQuestions","/body/functionalDefinition","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/3","/body/constraints/4","/body/constraints/5","/body/constraints/6","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/citations/9","/citations/10","/citations/11","/citations/12","/citations/13","/citations/14","/citations/15","/citations/16","/citations/17","/citations/18","/citations/19","/citations/20","document:line:26","document:line:301","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-framework.md — scope/depth policy, citations, recursive execution and accuracy convention","design/analyze-context-builder.md — lossless relevance window, ownership, caching and failure contracts","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — incremental child plans, per-plan validation, depth ceilings, persistence and partial failures","CLAUDE.md — accuracy, provider access and trailing structural reference","site/analyze.html:61 — exploration-grounded claims",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-12f70133491114c9.json — excluded graph-edge defects","src/analyze/measure.ts — measured sizing, unknown counts and caller hints","src/analyze/planner/scope-band.ts — existing per-plan task bands","src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1590 — broad-request pipeline and measured scope","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:727 — source-hinted intent handling","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/source-modules.ts — directory modules and stored-module ownership","src/analyze/explore — cited lookup limits, content cuts and completeness records","src/analyze/runtimes/data/discovery-objects.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/infra/_shared.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/infra/discovery-families.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/code/adherence-check.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/data/adherence-check.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/infra/adherence-check.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/docs/family-summarise.ts","src/analyze/docs-retrieval.ts","src/analyze/summariser/driver.ts","src/analyze/planner/schema.ts","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.code.system.md — retained answer caps and exploration shapes","src/daemon/tools/builtins/search/grep.ts — shared caller limits and omission reporting","src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts — process and output limits","src/analyze/__tests__/measure-pass.test.ts — acceptance-case inventory, including sampled stores and unknown sizes","src/analyze/explore/__tests__/completeness-all-lookups.test.ts — completeness and relationship-evidence case inventory","git commit 83a1cc0 — steering-only change and historical c2/c11 source","git commit 990a5fceb — removal of the historical scope picker"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Add stable functional-requirement identifiers for s8 and s9; the flattened functional definition currently stops at s7, although both newer stories have substantive acceptance criteria.","Label the problem statement and c2/c11 references as the historical baseline. Current measurement and broad-request code already implements parts of that baseline's proposed corrections.","Update the resolved hook question's explanation to reflect that steering was applied separately: it still says Story s5 changes the steering block, whereas the current s5 concerns answer layouts and steering is explicitly a non-goal.","Carry the revised root-based depth policy into the upstream plan-builder documentation when implemented; it currently permits deeper L/XL recursion. Historical external measurements were assessed as recorded evidence; replaying those runs is optional for this scope assessment."]},{"chunkId":"broad","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were inspected against the live DEF, canonical artifact, upstream designs, and relevant runtime and test sources. The s6–s8 capability boundaries and module-discovery approach are feasible, but s7's unconditional completion promises conflict with s9's budget-stopped outcome. No visual artifact is attached to this DEF; prose is sufficient for this epic-level scope.","findings":[{"id":"broad2-terminal-contract-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/0","message":"Reconcile s7's lifecycle acceptance with s9's new budget-exhaustion outcome. s7/ac1 requires every stage to complete, s7/ac2 requires nested steps to run and reach the final report, and S007:FR001 repeats the unconditional completion promise. An accepted plan stopped by s9/ac4 deliberately leaves work unexecuted, even when no task fails. S007:FR003 qualifies completion only for the docs aggregation and code-module prerequisites; neither covers this new outcome. Distinguish full completion from an explicitly incomplete terminal report, qualify the nested-execution promise accordingly, and specify whether retrieving that terminal report under the same run follows s7/ac4's stored-result behavior.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/0",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/1",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/3",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/29",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/31","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:235","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E2026