leteness and terminal schema-failure evidence","src/daemon/steps/analyze-step/answer-turn.ts — missing-prompt and answer-step failure contracts","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.code.system.md — failed lookups and model-directed coverage disclosures","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.data.system.md — failed versus empty data-source results","src/prompts/analyze/synthesize.adherence.system.md — omitted and partly read search evidence","src/analyze/explore/__tests__/completeness-all-lookups.test.ts:375 — exact/unknown totals, source limits, returned counts and partial-read assertions","src/daemon/steps/__tests__/analyze-step-bundle-report.test.ts — delivered report propagation and rejection of forged completeness","src/analyze/context/__tests__/answer-failure-mapping.test.ts — evidence, uncovered parts and cause chains preserved through both failure mappings","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/nested-aggregate-failure.test.ts:52 — nested failures and handling disclosures reach the final report","src/analyze/runtimes/__tests__/completeness-all-runtimes.test.ts — runtime completeness and sampling test inventory"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Extend regression assertions for the revised unknown-total rule to unreadable and skipped sources without a reached limit: buildCompleteness currently defaults total to returned in that case unless the caller explicitly supplies null.","Tests were inspected as evidence; executing tests or live-store analyses was unnecessary for this read-only DEF assessment."]},{"chunkId":"sizing","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were inspected against the live DEF, canonical artifact, upstream designs, and relevant planner, executor and test contracts. Measured sizing, caller hints, unknown-size fallback and sampling exceptions are coherent. The revised s9 prerequisites are feasible. Two acceptance inconsistencies remain around budget-stopped coverage and the timed completion benchmark. No visual artifact is attached or necessary for this epic-level capability definition.","findings":[{"id":"sizing2-budget-coverage-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","message":"Explicitly reporting budget exhaustion fixes silent termination, but the resulting coverage exception still contradicts the complete-handling requirements. A healthy run must stop with obtainable work unprocessed under s9/ac4, while FR003, s3/ac2 and s4/ac5 require full processing. k1 and the non-goal excluding time/model-cost reduction further constrain this tradeoff. Reconcile these requirements by explicitly distinguishing successful complete processing from budget-stopped incomplete termination, and state whether uncovered work can subsequently be completed.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:31 — FR003 requires processing oversized results in full","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:162 — s3/ac2 requires every part to be processed","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:187 — s4/ac5 requires every obtainable result to be processed","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:270 — s9/ac4 requires termination with uncovered work","design/analyze-context-builder.md:167 — accuracy-first, lossless inclusion contract"]},{"id":"sizing2-timed-completion-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","message":"The revised criterion makes the revision, predetermined XL limit and measurement interval observable, but only requires a final report within that limit. Because ac4 now expressly produces a final report on budget exhaustion, this benchmark can pass after doing little work and returning an incomplete report. That does not demonstrate the docs end-to-end completion promised by s3/ac7 and s9's user value. Require this benchmark to finish the intended analysis without budget-induced uncovered work, while testing incomplete budget termination separately.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:167 — s3/ac7 closes the broad docs completion exception","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts:40 — existing broad docs regression","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts:62 — existing assertions require a report but only check that completeness is boolean"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/8","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/1","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/12","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/13","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:11 — incremental child-plan model","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:83 — independently measured per-plan task bands","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:138 — corrective retry contract","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:155 — XL partition children","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:194 — root scope depth ceilings","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:246 — resumability and persisted child plans","design/analyze-framework.md:36 — five-size depth policy","design/analyze-framework.md:488 — root-owned depth configuration","design/analyze-context-builder.md:167","CLAUDE.md:11","docs/daemon.md:758 — measurement, hints, fallback and sampling contracts","docs/daemon.md:930 — sizing reported on both paths","src/analyze/measure.ts","src/analyze/planner/recursive.ts","src/analyze/planner/scope-band.ts","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts:159","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts:208","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:443","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts:345","src/analyze/__tests__/measure.test.ts","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/run-measure.test.ts","src/analyze/planner/__tests__/recursive.test.ts:384","src/analyze/planner/__tests__/recursive.test.ts:500","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["In the downstream design, identify the aggregate-validation boundary and correction owner. Upstream documents describe children appearing during execution, whereas the current orchestrator builds the tree before execution. Specify how an aggregate overflow feeds correction without silently discarding children, and how the new root-wide limit relates to independently measured local task bands.","Record s9's two-level XL/L restriction as an intentional replacement of the upstream depth policy. Retain independent child measurement, explain precedence over configurable root ceilings, and clarify what keeping the existing XS policy preserves; M/S recursion should remain bounded by the root ceiling.","Define one root-owned execution budget shared by descendants, including accounting across restart, and explain how final reporting is completed after exhaustion. The timed benchmark should record the revision, policy limit, elapsed interval, maximum depth, executed task count and coverage outcome.","No live benchmark was executed during this read-only DEF review; execution evidence belongs to implementation acceptance."]},{"chunkId":"handling","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed. The revised small-request criterion correctly distinguishes measured size from model-call capacity. Whole-item processing, retained findings and citations, sequential calls, and failed-part reporting are coherent at DEF level. Complete-processing obligations still conflict with s9's budget termination. No additional diagram or UX artifact is necessary for this capability at this stage.","findings":[{"id":"handling2-budget-completeness-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1","message":"s3 requires every partition to be processed and combined without losing findings, while FR003 and S003:FR002 repeat unconditional complete processing. Under s9/ac4, an otherwise healthy run must stop when its budget is reached and leave work uncovered. Reporting that outcome honestly satisfies disclosure but does not satisfy these processing requirements. Explicitly distinguish complete execution from budget-stopped incomplete execution across s3 and its flattened requirements. Also clarify that an incomplete terminal report does not, by itself, demonstrate closure of the docs aggregation exception in ac7 and S003:FR005.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/15",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/18",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:162","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:167","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:270","design/analyze-context-builder.md:167 — accuracy-first, lossless inclusion contract"]}],"inspected