small-request handling on complete input fitting a model call and permits reported, complete partitioning otherwise.","s4/ac2 adds confirmation that the indexed location still holds the item and uncovered reporting for unconfirmed, missing or unreadable content.","s4/ac5 now requires processing obtainable results while preserving sampled, failed and uncovered-source disclosures; flattened S004:FR001 gains the sampling qualification.","s5 now depends on s1, s2, s3 and s4. Its enumeration criterion, local requirement and flattened S005:FR001 now qualify coverage by established evidence and disclose sampled, failed or uncovered sources.","s9 gains dependencies on s2, s3 and s7. Its XL/L policy permits children but prohibits further children beneath them; aggregate validation counts root and descendant tasks, with a policy for every size and existing XS policy retained.","s9 budget exhaustion now produces an explicitly incomplete terminal report retaining findings and listing uncovered work. Its docs timing criterion specifies a stated revision, an XL policy limit fixed before execution and the request-to-report interval.","The sampling citation id changes from c21 to c22; the existing triage citation already uses c22, so citation identity and all dependent evidence references require fresh assessment.","Current inventory adds document:line:301 for Resolved questions: 127 units versus 126 previously, with no removed units. The functionalDefinition still contains requirements only; no new structured visual definition appears in the canonical body."],"directChunkIds":["scope","reporting","sizing","handling","retrieval","answers"],"indirectChunkIds":["broad"],"rationale":"Use full mode because all seven substantive capabilities are affected directly or through shared contracts. The unchanged broad-request chunk cannot safely retain its prior pass: s9 changes permitted nested execution, terminal outcomes, report contents and timing for the same lifecycle that s7 promises will complete and replay. Revised totals, pointer validation and qualified enumeration also change downstream reporting and coverage expectations. The upstream plan-builder permits independently measured L children for XL partitions and deeper recursion under root ceilings; its persistence and partial-failure contracts must be reconciled with the revised depth and budget policies. The unchanged complete-processing requirements, accuracy non-goal, source ownership, directory-module compatibility, docs exception and tests remain part of that assessment. This is an epic DEF with no required workflow ancestors supplied; cited upstream designs remain applicable, while downstream HLD/LLD/PLAN/BUILD artifacts are not required. The prior accepted report found no necessary attached visual; current preparation found no added structured visual definition, but fresh chunks must independently assess linked or necessary visuals and inspect actual renderings where applicable. All prior findings remain effective pending fresh inspection. No coverage is retained, no historical result is submitted as a new review, and final consistency is fresh.","chunkMapping":[{"priorIds":["scope"],"currentIds":["scope"],"explanation":"Same capability boundary, expanded by the newly inventoried resolved-questions section. Changed citation identity, story ordering and execution policy require fresh review."},{"priorIds":["broad"],"currentIds":["broad"],"explanation":"Same selectors and foundational capability grouping. Although their text is unchanged, revised budget and depth behavior affects lifecycle completion, nested evidence and persisted results; the prior pass is not retained."},{"priorIds":["reporting"],"currentIds":["reporting"],"explanation":"Same selectors; unknown-total wording changes directly and budget, stale-pointer and coverage qualifications affect shared result and answer contracts."},{"priorIds":["sizing"],"currentIds":["sizing"],"explanation":"Same s2/s9 grouping; revised prerequisites, child-depth policy, aggregate counting, budget termination and timing acceptance require complete fresh assessment."},{"priorIds":["handling"],"currentIds":["handling"],"explanation":"Same selectors; capacity-aware small-request handling changes directly, while s9 budgets and depth restrictions affect complete partition processing and aggregation."},{"priorIds":["retrieval"],"currentIds":["retrieval"],"explanation":"Same selectors; pointer confirmation, incomplete-source handling and flattened sampling requirements change directly."},{"priorIds":["answers"],"currentIds":["answers"],"explanation":"Same selectors; prerequisites and evidence-qualified enumeration change directly, with additional downstream effects from incomplete budget reports."},{"priorIds":["consistency"],"currentIds":["consistency"],"explanation":"Same final reconciliation role, freshly dependent on all seven current substantive assessments. No substantive chunks were added, removed, split or merged."}],"retainedCoverage":[],"carriedFindingIds":["[1,\"scope\",\"scope-order-01\"]","[1,\"scope\",\"scope-budget-02\"]","[1,\"scope\",\"scope-citation-03\"]","[1,\"reporting\",\"reporting-unknown-total-01\"]","[1,\"sizing\",\"sizing-prerequisites-01\"]","[1,\"sizing\",\"sizing-budget-completeness-02\"]","[1,\"sizing\",\"sizing-aggregate-policy-03\"]","[1,\"sizing\",\"sizing-timing-acceptance-04\"]","[1,\"handling\",\"handling-small-fit-01\"]","[1,\"retrieval\",\"retrieval-stale-pointer-01\"]","[1,\"retrieval\",\"retrieval-sampling-completeness-02\"]","[1,\"answers\",\"answers-prerequisites-01\"]","[1,\"answers\",\"answers-completeness-02\"]"],"consistencyChunkIds":["consistency"]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"impact","phase":"impact","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"scope","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"broad","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"reporting","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"sizing","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"handling","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"retrieval","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"answers","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":2,"retriesUsed":1,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Status contradicts findings or mandatory verification limits: received changes_requested, expected passed; limitations=0, HIGH/MED=0"}],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"analyzer-def-s9-r1","attempt":2,"artifactId":"DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574","status":"changes_requested","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":6,"LOW":0},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the live DEF, canonical artifact, recorded requirements, cited repository evidence and upstream designs. Rollout prerequisites are now coherent, but citation identity and budget-versus-completeness requirements still need reconciliation. No authored or generated visual is attached or necessary for this epic-level definition.","findings":[{"id":"scope2-citation-01","severity":"MED","location":"/citations/20/id","message":"Renaming the sampling decision to c22 creates another collision: citations/19 already uses c22 for the triage record. The two distinct evidence records therefore cannot be addressed uniquely in either the canonical artifact or Markdown. Assign the sampling decision an unused identity while preserving the existing triage citation.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/19",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/citations/20","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:294","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:295","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:327","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:328"]},{"id":"scope2-budget-contract-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2","message":"The new budget-exhaustion outcome is explicit, but its exception has not been reconciled with the complete-processing requirements. FR003 requires oversized inputs to be processed in full; s3/ac2 requires every part to be reasoned over; and s4/ac5 requires every obtainable result to be processed. A healthy run that reaches s9/ac4's budget must instead stop with work unprocessed. Define which completeness obligations apply to successful runs and explicitly qualify them for budget-stopped runs across the functional definition and story criteria, so acceptance does not simultaneously require both outcomes.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/4",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:31","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:162","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:187","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:270"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/flavor","/body/problem","/body/nonGoals","/body/assumptions","/body/constraints","/body/stories","/body/openQuestions","/body/functionalDefinition","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/body/constraints/3","/body/constraints/4","/body/constraints/5","/body/constraints/6","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/citations/9","/citations/10","/citations/11","/citations/12","/citations/13","/citations/14","/citations/15","/citations/16","/citations/17","/citations/18","/citations/19","/citations/20","document:line:26","document:line:301","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-framework.md — scope/depth policy, citations, recursive execution and accuracy convention","design/analyze-context-builder.md — lossless relevance window, ownership, caching and failure contracts","design/analyze-plan-builder.md — incremental child plans, per-plan validation, depth ceilings, persistence and partial failures","CLAUDE.md — accuracy, provider access and trailing structural reference","site/analyze.html:61 — exploration-grounded claims",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-12f70133491114c9.json — excluded graph-edge defects","src/analyze/measure.ts — measured sizing, unknown counts and caller hints","src/analyze/planner/scope-band.ts — existing per-plan task bands","src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1590 — broad-request pipeline and measured scope","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:727 — source-hinted intent handling","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/source-modules.ts — directory modules and stored-module ownership","src/analyze/