s__/dropped-or-failed.test.ts","Citation c1 inventory: inspected limit, sampling and completeness sites in its named exploration, retrieval, summariser and plan-runtime files"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Retain the registry-wide lookup coverage test and propagation tests for both analyzer paths as regression evidence. Tests were inspected, not executed, during this read-only design review."]},{"chunkId":"sizing","status":"passed","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed. Measured sizing, entry-point parity, caller hints, reported counts and conservative unknown-size fallback form a coherent DEF-level contract. The Redis/etcd sampling decision is compatible with XL fallback without exhaustive key scans. Current code supports integration feasibility; cited sizing behavior is historical. No visual artifact is attached or necessary for this capability.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/1","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/12","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/13","/citations/1","/citations/7","/citations/10","/citations/20","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","DEF.md:133-149 — sizing prerequisites and all five acceptance criteria","DEF.md:181-187,295 — sampling exception and stakeholder sizing decision","DEF.md:263-271 — downstream size-policy consumers","design/analyze-framework.md:36-68 — measured buckets, depth policy and intent","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:75-83,155-194 — per-plan sizing and root depth policy","docs/daemon.md:758-850 — thresholds, counting bases, hints and unknown-size fallback","src/analyze/measure.ts — shared counting functions, thresholds, fallback and sampled-source handling","src/analyze/context/request.ts — shared MCP request construction and caller hints","src/daemon/steps/analyze-step/phases/start.ts:60-74 — scope resolution and measurement before planning","src/daemon/steps/analyze-step/phases/plan.ts — measured request size passed to exploration execution","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:374-396 — measurement before run planning and persistence","src/analyze/__tests__/measure.test.ts — threshold boundaries, scoped counts, hints and reporting assertions","src/analyze/__tests__/measure-pass.test.ts:111-145,329-378 — area-sensitive sizing, unknown counts and sampled live stores","src/daemon/steps/__tests__/analyze-step-measure.test.ts:108-226 — measured planning size and hint propagation","git show 990a5fceb^:src/analyze/classifier/scope-picker.ts — historical repository counts and model-picked sizing","git show 62ccb3100^:src/mcp/analyze-step/phases/start.ts — former MCP path before relocation"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Label c2 and c11 as historical baseline references and pin their source revision. The scope picker was removed, and the MCP start handler moved into the daemon; current code already measures size.","When refining acceptance fixtures, use the same question over different scoped areas within one repository, then vary unrelated repository content while holding the area fixed. This distinguishes actual scope measurement from wording and repository-wide sizing.","Make the pre-plan area measurement and post-lookup result measurement explicit in downstream contracts and reports. Preserve their separate bases, and ensure a small returned sample cannot replace the conservative XL policy for Redis or etcd.","Tests and live analyses were not executed during this read-only DEF review; source contracts and relevant assertions were inspected."]},{"chunkId":"handling","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed. Story s3 covers both paths, small requests with oversized input, whole-item reading, lossless combination, failed-part disclosure and the s7 docs exception. Its unconditional coverage requirements still conflict with s9's budget-stopped outcome.","findings":[{"id":"handling3-budget-coverage-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1","message":"s3/ac2 requires every part to be processed without losing findings, and FR003 and S003:FR002 require processing in full. However, s9/ac4 requires an otherwise healthy run to terminate with work uncovered when its size-based budget is reached. Honest disclosure does not satisfy the unconditional processing requirement. Reconcile complete processing with budget-stopped execution across s3 and its flattened requirements, including whether uncovered work can subsequently complete. Also require the oversized docs scenario in ac7/S003:FR005 to demonstrate completed coverage: an incomplete terminal report alone must not count as closing s7's aggregation exception.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/15",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/18",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:162","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:167","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:270","design/analyze-context-builder.md — Sizing: lossless inclusion and accuracy-first contract"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/2","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/5","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/6","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/14","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/15","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/16","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/17","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/18","/citations/3","/citations/9","/citations/15","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","design/analyze-context-builder.md","design/analyze-plan-builder.md","design/analyze-framework.md:240","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/docs/family-summarise.ts","src/analyze/summariser/driver.ts","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":["When refining acceptance tests, include a relationship spanning two partitions and a finding near the end of an oversized item; verify retained source provenance and sequential model calls. The DEF's prose is adequate for this stage; no interaction or UX definitions or companions are attached to it."]},{"chunkId":"planning","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed. Whole-request depth inheritance, recursive task counting, XS preservation, prerequisites, and incomplete budget termination are now explicit. The XL timing criterion still permits budget-stopped analysis to satisfy the completion benchmark.","findings":[{"id":"planning-xl-completion-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","message":"ac5 requires a final report within the predetermined XL time limit, but ac4 expressly produces an incomplete report when that budget is exhausted. A run can therefore leave most work uncovered and still pass the timing benchmark. This does not establish the completed broad analysis promised by s9's user value and s3/ac7. Require the benchmark to finish its intended coverage wit