o longer exists at its recorded path.","Carry the replacement root-depth policy into applicable upstream documentation when implemented. Historical external session logs were assessed as recorded observations; replaying those measurements is optional for this scope review."]},{"chunkId":"broad","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the live DEF, canonical artifact, upstream designs and relevant runtime/test sources. The s6–s8 dependency order is feasible, and the docs and code-module exceptions have explicit closure owners. One lifecycle acceptance conflict requires correction. No visual artifact is attached or necessary for this epic-level capability definition.","findings":[{"id":"broad3-terminal-contract-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/0","message":"Reconcile s7's completion contract with s9's budget-stopped outcome. s7/ac1 requires every stage to complete, s7/ac2 requires nested steps to run and reach the report, and S007:FR001 repeats unconditional completion. However, s9/ac4 requires an accepted broad run to stop with work unexecuted when its budget is reached. S007:FR003 qualifies completion only for docs aggregation and code-module prerequisites. Define the distinction between full completion and an incomplete terminal report, qualify nested-execution acceptance accordingly, and specify whether retrieving a budget-stopped report under the same run follows s7/ac4's stored-result behavior.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/0",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/1",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/6/acceptanceCriteria/3",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/29",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/31","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E202