ions","src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1590–1675 — unfocused run-mode entry and cause-specific outcomes","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:170–440 — terminal failures, stored-result replay and source-hinted requests","src/analyze/orchestrator/persistence.ts — abandoned-run records and persistence behavior","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts:343–395 — nested execution and child report propagation","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/source-modules.ts — directory identity, containment, ownership, language selection and missing-target errors","src/analyze/runtimes/code/discovery-modules.ts — directory discovery and stored-module compatibility","src/analyze/runtimes/code/structure-module-tree.ts:105–205 — module identity, longest-directory ownership and directed import edges","src/analyze/runtimes/code/surface-functional.ts — directory and entity-id inputs, recursive surfaces and explicit refusals","src/analyze/runtimes/shared/__tests__/source-modules.test.ts:47–130 — directory membership, mixed languages, stored ownership and path identity assertions","src/analyze/runtimes/code/__tests__/module-directories.test.ts:363–435 — recursive surfaces, path forms and missing-target assertions","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/hinted-branch.test.ts:68–103 — focused/unfocused source hints and invalid pairings","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/shaper-causes.test.ts:56 — cause-specific terminal failure assertions","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/orchestrator.test.ts:489–541 — completed-run replay assertions","src/daemon/__tests__/analyze-run-abandoned.test.ts:63–88 — terminal abandonment and persisted record assertions","src/indexer/parser/typescript.ts — module-entity occurrence inspection","src/indexer/parser/python.ts — shared-namespace module entities","src/indexer/parser/go.ts — shared-namespace module entities","src/indexer/parser/java.ts — package/import module entities with empty repository and file","src/indexer/parser/scala.ts — package/import module entities with empty repository and file"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Use explicit acceptance fixtures for mixed-language directories, descendant-only source, overlapping stored modules, and relative versus absolute module values; the shared runtime provides concrete rules for these cases.","Tests and live analyses were not executed. This read-only DEF review inspected source contracts and assertions."]},{"chunkId":"completeness","status":"passed","summary":"All assigned units were assessed. The completeness contracts cover both analyzer paths, known and unknown totals, sampling, partial reads, omitted files, failed versus empty results, and preservation of exploration evidence when synthesis fails. Completeness claims are appropriately bounded by available evidence and the graph-repair exclusion. No blocking design defect was demonstrated. No visual artifact is necessary for this assignment.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/0/acceptanceCriteria/5","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/0","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/7","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/8","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/9","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/10","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/11","/citations/0","/citations/4","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","design/analyze-context-builder.md:167-182","design/analyze-framework.md:250-266","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:258-266","src/analyze/completeness.ts","src/analyze/explore/completeness-facts.ts","src/analyze/explore/answer-report.ts","src/analyze/explore/types.ts","src/analyze/context/driver.ts:1730-1858","src/analyze/executor/plan-sources.ts","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:430-640","src/daemon/steps/analyze-step/phases/bundle.ts:85-230","src/daemon/tools/builtins/search/grep.ts","src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts:183-215","src/analyze/explore/__tests__/completeness-all-lookups.test.ts:271-298","src/analyze/context/__tests__/pipeline-outcome.test.ts:599-650","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/run-report.test.ts:160-231","src/daemon/steps/__tests__/analyze-step-bundle-report.test.ts","src/daemon/steps/__tests__/analyze-step-failed-lookup.test.ts:125-175","src/daemon/steps/__tests__/analyze-step-answer-prompt-missing.test.ts:111-160","src/analyze/runtimes/__tests__/partly-read-plan-tasks.test.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/__tests__/dropped-or-failed.test.ts","Citation c1 inventory: inspected limit, sampling and completeness sites in its named exploration, retrieval, summariser and plan-runtime files"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Retain the registry-wide lookup coverage test and propagation tests for both analyzer paths as regression evidence. Tests were inspected, not executed, during this read-only design review."]},{"chunkId":"sizing","status":"passed","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed. Measured sizing, entry-point parity, caller hints, reported counts and conservative unknown-size fallback form a coherent DEF-level contract. The Redis/etcd sampling decision is compatible with XL fallback without exhaustive key scans. Current code supports integration feasibility; cited sizing behavior is historical. No visual artifact is attached or necessary for this capability.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/1/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/1","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/12","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/13","/citations/1","/citations/7","/citations/10","/citations/20","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","DEF.md:133-149 — sizing prerequisites and all five acceptance criteria","DEF.md:181-187,295 — sampling exception and stakeholder sizing decision","DEF.md:263-271 — downstream size-policy consumers","design/analyze-framework.md:36-68 — measured buckets, depth policy and intent","design/analyze-plan-builder.md:75-83,155-194 — per-plan sizing and root depth policy","docs/daemon.md:758-850 — thresholds, counting bases, hints and unknown-size fallback","src/analyze/measure.ts — shared counting functions, thresholds, fallback and sampled-source handling","src/analyze/context/request.ts — shared MCP request construction and caller hints","src/daemon/steps/analyze-step/phases/start.ts:60-74 — scope resolution and measurement before planning","src/daemon/steps/analyze-step/phases/plan.ts — measured request size passed to exploration execution","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:374-396 — measurement before run planning and persistence","src/analyze/__tests__/measure.test.ts — threshold boundaries, scoped counts, hints and reporting assertions","src/analyze/__tests__/measure-pass.test.ts:111-145,329-378 — area-sensitive sizing, unknown counts and sampled live stores","src/daemon/steps/__tests__/analyze-step-measure.test.ts:108-226 — measured planning size and hint propagation","git show 990a5fceb^:src/analyze/classifier/scope-picker.ts — historical repository counts and model-picked sizing","git show 62ccb3100^:src/mcp/analyze-step/phases/start.ts — former MCP path before relocation"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Label c2 and c11 as historical baseline references and pin their source revision. The scope picker was removed, and the MCP start handler moved into the daemon; current code already measures size.","When refining acceptance fixtures, use the same question over different scoped areas within one repository, then vary unrelated repository content while holding the area fixed. This distinguishes actual scope measurement from wording and repository-wide sizing.","Make the pre-plan area measurement and post-lookup result measurement explicit in downstream contracts and reports. Preserve their separate bases, and ensure a small returned sample cannot replace the conservative XL policy for Redis or etcd.","Tests and live analyses were not executed during this read-only DEF review; source contracts and relevant assertions were inspected."]},{"chunkId":"handling","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed. Story s3 covers both paths, small requests with oversized input, whole-item reading, lossless combination, failed-part disclosure and the s7 docs exception. Its unconditional coverage requirements still conflict with s9's budget-stopped outcome.","findings":[{"id":"handling3-budget-coverage-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1","message":"s3/ac2 requires every part to be processed without losing findings, and FR003 and S003:FR002 require processing in full. However, s9/ac4 requires an otherwise healthy run to terminate with work uncovered when its size-based budget is reached. Honest disclosure does not satisfy the unconditional processing requirement. Reconcile complete processing with budget-stopped execution across s3 and its flattened requirements, including whether uncovered work can subsequently complete. Also require the oversized docs scenario in ac7/S003:FR005 to demonstrate completed coverage: an incomplete terminal report alone must not count as closing s7's aggregation exception.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/15",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/18",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:162","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:167","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:270","design/analyze-context-builder.md — Sizing: lossless inclusion and accuracy-first contract"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/2","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/5","/body/stories/2/acceptanceCriteria/6","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/2","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/14","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/15","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/16","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/17","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/18","/citations/3","/citations/9","/citations/15","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json","design/analyze-context-builder.md","design/analyze-plan-builder.md","design/analyze-framework.md:240","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts","src/analyze/runtimes/docs/family-summarise.ts","src/analyze/summariser/driver.ts","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":["When refining acceptance tests, include a relationship spanning two partitions and a finding near the end of an oversized item; verify retained source provenance and sequential model calls. The DEF's prose is adequate for this stage; no interaction or UX definitions or companions are attached to it."]},{"chunkId":"planning","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed. Whole-request depth inheritance, recursive task counting, XS preservation, prerequisites, and incomplete budget termination are now explicit. The XL timing criterion still permits budget-stopped analysis to satisfy the completion benchmark.","findings":[{"id":"planning-xl-completion-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","message":"ac5 requires a final report within the predetermined XL time limit, but ac4 expressly produces an incomplete report when that budget is exhausted. A run can therefore leave most work uncovered and still pass the timing benchmark. This does not establish the completed broad analysis promised by s9's user value and s3/ac7. Require the benchmark to finish its intended coverage without budget-induced omissions; test budget-stopped reporting separately. Existing source-coverage limitations can remain disclosed without requiring an unsupported claim that the underlying index is complete.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json#/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:261","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md:167","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts:40 — the existing regression requires a report but accepts either completeness value"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/8","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/8/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/constraints/0","/body/constraints/1","/body/constraints/2","/citations/9","/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/DEF.md",".insrc/artifacts/DEF-b9d5c5c40df5a574.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/analyzer-def-s9-r1.json","design/analyze-plan-builder.md","design/analyze-framework.md","design/analyze-context-builder.md:167","CLAUDE.md:11","src/analyze/planner/recursive.ts","src/analyze/planner/scope-band.ts","src/analyze/planner/validate.ts","src/analyze/planner/driver.ts","src/analyze/planner/__tests__/recursive.test.ts","src/analyze/executor/walker.ts:343","src/analyze/executor/plan-sources.ts","src/analyze/orchestrator/driver.ts:437","src/analyze/orchestrator/__tests__/docs-broad-live.test.ts","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/S009/EXT.md","docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/S007/measurements/live-runs-t17.md"],"limitations":[],"advice":["In subsequent design and tests, cover aggregate-limit crossing when a later child is generated, correction exhaustion, and preservation of earlier findings. Distinguish the new whole-tree cap from existing per-plan bands.","Record the exact benchmark request, model/provider configuration, index state, policy values, and cache conditions alongside the revision and timing. No live benchmark was executed during this read-only design review."]},{"chunkId":"retrieval","status":"passed","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed against the current DEF, canonical artifact, upstream designs and relevant source contracts. Retrieval requirements cover both analyzer paths, prerequisite ordering, validated source reads, shared-search compatibility and disclosed sampling exceptions. No blocking design defect was demonstrated. No diagram or UX artifact is necessary for this capability at DEF stage.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/stories/3","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/0","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/1","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/2","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/3","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/4","/body/stories/3/acceptanceCriteria/5","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/3","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/19","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/20","/body/functionalDefinition/requirements/21","/body/functionalDe