es, functional-requirement entries or inventory selectors are added or removed. The functional definition remains requirements-only, with no attached visual definitions or companions."],"directChunkIds":["scope","broad","sizing","handling","planning","retrieval"],"indirectChunkIds":["completeness","answers"],"rationale":"Full review is appropriate because the revised budget exception and terminal lifecycle affect every capability, even where wording is unchanged. Scope owns the aggregate requirements and constraints; broad owns terminal state, nested propagation and immutable replay; handling owns full processing and docs-exception closure; planning owns the budget and successful XL benchmark; retrieval directly changes its processing criterion; sizing directly references the renamed sampling citation and supplies the size that controls execution budgets. Unchanged completeness and answer requirements must now account for work never executed, retained findings and replayed incomplete reports. The context-builder's lossless relevance contract, plan-builder's incrementally generated children, per-plan counts, root-depth ceilings and terminal aggregation remain applicable upstream evidence. S009/EXT.md supplies the originating size/budget intent. These dependencies require fresh reconciliation of acceptance scenarios, persistence contracts, ownership, source coverage and test evidence, including unchanged directory-module compatibility and whole-item requirements. The current envelope has no attachments and the body has no visual definitions beyond the requirements container; substantive review must still independently assess necessary visuals and inspect actual renderings if relevant artifacts are discovered. Attempt 3 is the immediately preceding complete same-party review, with no limitations and five effective findings. All five are carried without resolving them during preparation. No coverage is retained from attempt 3, no invalidated attempt 2 result is reused, 